hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, Isa ibn Jariya informed us, from Jabir, who said: Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind and my house is far. He spoke to him about prayer, asking concession to pray in his house. He said: Do you hear the call to prayer? He said: Yes. He said: Come to it, even if crawling."
"1802","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, Isa ibn Jariya narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs. Ibn Umm Maktum came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my house is far and I have a dog. He gave him concession for some days, then ordered it to be killed."
"1803","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, there is reward for him in it, and whatever beasts eat from it, meaning birds and predators, is charity for him."
"1804","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqala, muzabana, mukhabara, mu'awama, and exception."
"1805","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade entering water except with a waist-wrapper."
"1806","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother when it has grown hair."
"1807","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, Abu Isma'il narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr and al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Mughith, from Jabir, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not give permission to one who does not begin with greeting."
"1808","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Malik, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hasten from the Black Stone until he reached the Black Stone for three circuits."
"1809","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick man, and I was with him. He saw him praying and prostrating upon a cushion, so he forbade him and said: If you can prostrate on the ground, then prostrate, otherwise gesture with a gesture, and make the prostration lower than the bowing."
"1810","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Sallam, meaning Ibn Sulaym, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to what will save you from your enemy and cause your provisions to flow to you? Supplicate to Allah in your night and day, for supplication is the weapon of the believer."
"1811","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir; Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may deny me while reclining on his couch, a narration from me reaching him, and he says: The Messenger of Allah did not say this; leave this and bring what is in the Qur'an. Isma'il said: I narrated it to Amr ibn Ubayd, and he said: No; al-Hasan narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah. He said: I said: Come with us to al-Hasan. So we went to al-Hasan and asked him about the narration, and he said: Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir."
"1812","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride the sacrificial animals in a proper manner until you find another mount."
"1813","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade charging a fee for the stallion's covering."
"1814","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade withholding surplus water in order to withhold pasture by it."
"1815","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Dhayyal ibn Harmala al-Asadi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: Quraysh gathered one day against the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Look for the most knowledgeable of you in magic, soothsaying, and poetry, and let him go to this man who has divided our ranks, scattered our affair, and disparaged our religion, and let him speak to him and see what he answers. They said: We know no one but Utba ibn Rabi'a. They said: You, O Abu al-Walid. So Utba came to him and said: O Muhammad, are you better, or Abdullah? The Messenger of Allah remained silent. Then he said: Are you better, or Abd al-Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. He said: If you claim that they are better than you, then they worshipped the gods you disparaged, and if you claim that you are better than them, then speak so we may hear your words. By Allah, we have never seen a young sheep more ill-omened for its people than you: you divided our ranks, scattered our affair, disparaged our religion, and disgraced us among the Arabs, until it spread among them that among Quraysh there is a sorcerer, and among Quraysh there is a soothsayer. By Allah, we await nothing but something like the cry of a woman in labor, that some of us will rise against others with swords until we annihilate one another. O man, if it is need that afflicts you, we will collect until you become the richest man of Quraysh, and if it is desire for marriage, choose whichever women of Quraysh you wish and we will marry you to ten. The Messenger of Allah said to him: Have you finished? He said: Yes. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate: Ha Mim, a revelation from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, until he reached: But if they turn away, then say: I warn you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud. Utba said: Enough, enough. Is there nothing with you besides this? He said: No. So he returned to Quraysh, and they said: What is behind you? He said: I left nothing that I thought you would address him with except that I addressed him with it. They said: Did he answer you? He said: Yes, by the One who set it up as a building, I understood nothing of what he said except that he said: I warn you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud. They said: Woe to you, a man speaks to you in Arabic and you do not know what he said? He said: No, by Allah, I understood nothing of what he said except the mention of the thunderbolt."
"1816","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Mecca, Abu Quhafa was brought, his head and beard like thaghama, and he said: Change the gray hair, but avoid black."
"1817","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Ibn Aqil, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call out, O Umar, among the people: that whoever dies worshipping Allah sincerely from his heart, Allah will admit him to Paradise and forbid the Fire for him. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not give the people glad tidings? He said: No, lest they rely on it."
"1818","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'ida, from Ibn Aqil, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: When do you pray witr? He said: At the beginning of the night, after the night prayer. Then he said to Umar: When do you pray witr? He said: At the end of the night. He said to Abu Bakr: You took the cautious way, and said to Umar: You took the strong way."
"1819","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Mufaddal ibn Faddala, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of a leper and placed it with him in the bowl, and said: Eat, in the name of Allah, trusting in Allah and relying upon Him."
"1820","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Sha'bi narrated to me, from Jabir, that two women of Hudhayl, one of them killed the other, and each of them had a husband and child. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed the blood money of the slain woman upon the clan of the killer, and absolved her husband and child. The clan of the slain woman said: Her inheritance is ours. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, her inheritance belongs to her husband and child. She was pregnant, and the clan of the slain woman said: She was pregnant and cast a fetus. The clan of the killer feared he would hold them liable, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, he neither drank, nor ate, nor cried out, so he did not raise his voice at birth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rhymed speech of the pre-Islamic age? And he judged for the fetus a ghurra: a male or female slave."
"1821","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us; Amr heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and a man of the Emigrants struck a man of the Helpers on the backside. The Ansari said: O Helpers! The Emigrant said: O Emigrants! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and said: What is this call of the pre-Islamic age? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, a man of the Emigrants struck a man of the Helpers on the backside. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it, for it is foul."
"1822","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us; Amr heard Jabir ibn Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold a mudabbar slave."
"1823","And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deception."
"1824","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us; Amr heard, from Jabir, who said: Mu'adh used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and lead his people. One night the Prophet delayed the prayer, so he came and recited Surah al-Baqara. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you a trial, O Mu'adh?"
"1825","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us; Amr heard, Jabir said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, meaning Abdullah ibn Ubayy, after he had been placed in his pit, ordered him brought out, blew upon him of his saliva, dressed him in his shirt, and Allah knows best."
"1826","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us; Amr heard, Jabir said: When there was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say: He is Able to send punishment upon you from above you, he said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or from beneath your feet, he said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or to clothe you in factions and make some of you taste the violence of others, he said: These two are easier, or lighter."
"1827","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us; Amr heard Jabir: A man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and he said: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Then pray two units."
"1828","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us; Amr heard, from Jabir: My two ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise."
"1829","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us; Amr heard, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fed us horse meat and forbade us the meat of domestic donkeys."
"1830","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us; he said: I said to Amr: Did you hear Jabir say: A man passed with arrows in the mosque, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to hold their blades? He said: Yes."
"1831","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us; Amr heard, Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mukhabara."
"1832","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Tariq judged that umra belongs to the heir, on the authority of the saying of Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1833","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr; he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you has land or date-palms, let him not sell it until he offers it to his partner."
"1834","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered licking the bowl and licking the fingers, for one does not know in which of that the blessing lies."
"1835","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Extinguish the lamps."
"1836","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We did not pledge to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unto death; we only pledged to him that we would not flee."
"1837","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a townsman selling for a Bedouin."
"1838","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw as though my neck was struck, or my head cut off. He said: Why does one of you report the devil's play with him?"
"1839","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"1840","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the slain of Uhud be returned to the places where they fell, though some of them had been carried to Medina, or whomever Allah willed among them."
"1841","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade coming to women at night. Jabir said: Then we came to them at night afterwards."
"1842","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling years in advance."
"1843","Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqala, muzabana, and mukhabara, and forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears, and that it not be sold except for dinars and dirhams, except araya."
"1844","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us; he said: Ja'far heard his father narrating to him, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour water over his head three times, meaning in ritual washing."
"1845","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"1846","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man shall spend the night with a woman in a house unless he is her husband or a mahram."
"1847","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of usury, its giver, its scribe, and its two witnesses, and said: They are equal."
"1848","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: We went out on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we returned, I hurried ahead on a slow camel of mine. A rider caught up with me from behind and prodded my camel with a spear he had, so my camel went as fine as any camel you ever saw. I turned, and behold, it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What hurries you? I said: I am newly married. He said: A virgin did you marry, or a previously married woman? I said: A previously married woman. He said: Why not a young girl, that you might play with her and she with you? When they returned, he said: Wait until we enter at night in the evening, so that the disheveled woman may comb herself and the one whose husband was absent may remove hair."
"1849","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is valid for its recipients."
"1850","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Layth informed us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he poured forth from Arafat: O people, upon you is calm and dignity, and let none of you kill one another."
"1851","Mus'ab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you for whom the Fire will be forbidden tomorrow? For every gentle, soft, close, easy person."
"1852","Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about faith. He said: Patience and tolerance."
"1853","Abu Hammam narrated to us, al-Mughira ibn Siqlab narrated to us, Ma'qil ibn Ubayd Allah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I guarantee Paradise for him."
"1854","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, al-Walid, a man of goodness and righteousness, narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say while upon his pulpit on a Friday: O people, repent to Allah before you die, hasten with righteous deeds, connect what is between you and your Lord by much remembrance of Him and much charity in secret and openly, and you will be rewarded, aided, and provided for. Know that Allah has made Friday obligatory upon you as a prescribed obligation on this day of mine, in this station of mine, in this month of mine, in this year of mine, until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever abandons it, in my lifetime or after my death, denying it or belittling it, may Allah not gather his affairs, nor bless him in his matter. Verily he has no prayer, verily he has no zakat, verily he has no pilgrimage, verily he has no fasting, verily he has no righteousness. Whoever repents, Allah turns to him. No woman shall lead a man, no Bedouin shall lead an Emigrant, and no wicked man shall lead a righteous man, except a ruler whose sword and whip are feared."
"1855","Isa ibn Salim narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I strive in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, until I am killed, shall I enter Paradise? He said: Yes, unless you owe a debt for which you have no payment with you."
"1856","Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw as though my head was cut off, or my neck was struck. He said: Why does one of you report the devil's play with him?"
"1857","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah said: No man shall spend the night with a woman in a house unless he is her husband or a mahram."
"1858","Ja'far ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Mahmud ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: We bought a cow in the time of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to share in it. It escaped from us and resisted us. A freedman of ours called Dhakwan confronted it with a sword in his hand while it roamed in the open ground. It hastened to a hill, and when it passed by him, he struck it with the sword at the base of its neck, or upon its neck, and cut it open with the sword, and it fell, and he did not reach its ritual slaughter in time. I went out, I and Abdullah ibn Thabit ibn al-Jidh', and we met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of its affair. He said: Eat. If any of these beasts escapes you, restrain it with whatever you restrain wild game."
"1859","Ja'far ibn Mihran narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Sahl Abu Layla, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: Marhab ibn al-Harith the Jew came out saying: Is there a challenger? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is for him? Muhammad ibn Maslama said: I, O Messenger of Allah; I, by Allah, the wronged avenger; they killed my brother yesterday. He said: Stand to him. O Allah, aid him. When the two drew near one another, a tree lay between them, and each began to take shelter by it from the other. Whenever he sheltered by it from him, he cut with his sword what was below it, until I saw it standing like a standing man, until each reached the other. Marhab charged him and struck, and he shielded himself with the buckler, so his sword fell into it and stuck, and the buckler gripped it and held it. Muhammad ibn Maslama struck him and killed him."
"1860","Ja'far ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from his father Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: We advanced with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not knowing of the ambush the people had hidden for us. We faced the valley of Hunayn in the darkness of dawn, a hollow valley of the valleys of Tihama, steep, into which they descend in a descent. He said: By Allah, the people followed one another knowing nothing, when suddenly the battalions attacked them from every side. The people did not wait but fled back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned aside to the right and said: Where, O people? I am the Messenger of Allah; I am Muhammad ibn Abdullah."
"1861","Ja'far narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from his father Jabir, who said: Before Hawazin was a bulky man upon a red camel, in his hand a black banner; when he caught up he thrust with it, and when something before him escaped him, he pushed it from behind him and pierced it. Ali ibn Abi Talib and a man of the Ansar both aimed for him, each wanting him. Ali struck the camel's hocks and it fell upon its rear, and the Ansari struck his leg and cut off his foot with half his shin, and it fell, and the people fought. When the rout occurred, Kalada came out, the brother of Safwan ibn Umayya, that day a polytheist within the respite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had granted him: Has magic not perished today? Safwan said to him: Be silent, may Allah break your mouth. By Allah, for a man of Quraysh to rule me is dearer to me than for a man of Hawazin to rule me."
"1862","Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the Negus, and I was in the second row."
"1863","Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdullah, the freedman of Ghufra, narrated to us, he said: I heard Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Safwan say: Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: O people, Allah has detachments of angels who alight and stand over gatherings of remembrance on earth. So graze in the gardens of Paradise. They said: Where are the gardens of Paradise, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Gatherings of remembrance. So go and return in the remembrance of Allah, and remind Him of yourselves. Whoever loves to know his station with Allah, let him look at how Allah's station is with him, for Allah places the servant where he places Him in himself."
"1864","Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Umar, freedman of Ghufra, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1865","Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: My father mentioned, from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted is Modest, Generous; He is shy to have His servant raise his hands to Him and return them empty with nothing in them."
"1866","Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: My father mentioned, from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from Jabir, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the market, a woman took hold of his mount's bridle while he was upon a donkey and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband does not approach me, so separate me from him. Her husband passed by, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: What is with you and her? She has come complaining of your coldness, complaining that you do not approach her? He said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who honored you, my last time with her was this very night. The woman wept and said: He lies. Separate me from him, for he is among the most hateful of Allah's creation to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then took his head and her head and brought them together, and said: O Allah, draw each of them near to his companion. Jabir said: We remained as long as Allah willed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed through the market, and there we were with a woman carrying tanned skins. When she saw him, she threw down the skins and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, no human that Allah created is dearer to me than him, except you. Ubayd Allah said: I do not think I heard it from my father."
"1867","Ubayd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Qurra narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a sheet at his death to write in it a document for his community, that they would neither go astray nor be led astray. There was noise in the house, and Umar ibn al-Khattab spoke, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejected it."
"1868","Ubayd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Qurra narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever ascends the pass, the pass of al-Mirar, there shall be removed from him what was removed from the Children of Israel. The first to ascend it were our cavalry, the cavalry of Banu al-Khazraj. The people followed in succession. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of you are forgiven except the owner of the red camel. We said: Come, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) may seek forgiveness for you. He said: By Allah, that I find my stray camel is dearer to me than that your companion seek forgiveness for me. And behold, he was a man seeking a stray camel."
"1869","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called at his death for a sheet to write in it a document after which they would neither go astray nor be led astray. There was noise in the house, and Umar ibn al-Khattab spoke, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejected it."
"1870","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing dates and raisins together."
"1871","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Mecca say: Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of wine, the sale of pigs, the sale of carrion, and the sale of idols. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of the fat of carrion, for we grease ships with it, oil skins with it, and light lamps with it? He said: May Allah fight the Jews. Allah forbade them its fats, so they took them, melted them, sold them, and ate their prices."
"1872","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sa'd al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Jabir, who said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at al-Husayn ibn Ali, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say it."
"1873","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Greeting with a single finger, gesturing with it, is the act of the Jews."
"1874","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from his father, from Amir, from Jabir, who said: When Ja'far arrived from Abyssinia, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced him."
"1875","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to attend with the polytheists their gatherings. He said: He heard two angels behind him, one of them saying to his companion: Let us go and stand behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The other said: How shall we stand behind him when his only recent contact was touching idols? He said: After that he never returned to attending with the polytheists their gatherings."
"1876","Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1877","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artat narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling date-palms for two or three years, forbade buying what is on the tops of date-palms for a measure of dates, and forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"1878","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid, meaning al-Thaqafi, narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the year of the conquest to Mecca in Ramadan, and fasted until he reached Kura' al-Ghamim. The people fasted, on foot and mounted. It was said to him: The people find fasting hard; they only watch what you do. He called for a cup and raised it to him until the people looked, then drank. Some people broke their fast and some fasted. It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Some of them fasted. He said: Those are the disobedient. The walkers among his companions gathered to him and lined up to him, and said: We expose ourselves to the supplications of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though the journey is hard and the distance long. He said to them: Seek help with trotting, for it cuts the land from you and you will be lightened by it. He said: So we did, and we were lightened by it."
"1879","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khattab al-Basri narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Arabs are humiliated, Islam is humiliated."
"1880","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened from stone to stone."
"1881","Sufyan ibn Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Makki, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We were on a journey, and a man fasted and fainted, and his companions stood over him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed and they said: He fasted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness."
"1882","Ja'far ibn Humayd al-Kufi narrated to us, Ya'qub, meaning al-Qummi, narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariya, from Jabir, who said: A man used to carry wine from Khaybar to Medina and sell it to the Muslims. He carried a sum of it and arrived in Medina with it. A Muslim man met him and said: O so-and-so, wine has been forbidden. So he set it down where he stopped, upon a hill, and covered it with garments. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, it reached me that wine has been forbidden. He said: Yes. He said: May I return it to the one I bought it from? He said: Returning it is not proper. He said: May I gift it to one who will recompense me for it? He said: No. He said: In it is wealth of orphans under my care. He said: When the wealth of Bahrayn comes to us, come to us and we shall compensate your orphans from their wealth. Then he announced in Medina. The man said: O Messenger of Allah, may we benefit from the skins? He said: Untie their mouths. So it poured out until it settled in the belly of the valley."
"1883","Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, from Isa, from Jabir, similar to the hadith of Abu al-Rabi' concerning the story of Ibn Umm Maktum. He said: Answer, even if crawling or dragging."
"1884","Ja'far narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, from Isa, from Jabir, similar to the hadith of Ibn Umm Maktum concerning dogs."
"1885","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud, from Amir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the chiefs of the Ansar, he said to them: You will shelter me and protect me. They said: What is for us? He said: Paradise is for you."
"1886","121 - (1888) - Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon standing, then a caravan came from Sham, so the people turned away until none remained except twelve men, so this verse in Al-Jumuah was revealed: {And when they see trade or amusement, they disperse to it and leave you standing}."
"1887","122 - (1889) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats from this garlic, onion, and leek, let him not come near us."
"1888","123 - (1890) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"1889","124 - (1891) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is long absent, let him not come to his family at night."
"1890","125 - (1892) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: Fever came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked permission to enter upon him. He said: Who are you? She said: I am Umm Mildam. He said: Will you go to the people of Quba? She said: Yes. So she went to them and they got fever and suffered severe hardship from it, so they complained to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what we suffered from fever. He said: If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah and He will remove it from you, and if you wish, it will be a purification. They said: No, rather let it be a purification for us."
"1891","126 - (1893) - Abu Khaythamah informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Harshness and hardness of hearts is toward the east, among Rabiah and Mudar, and faith is among the people of Hijaz."
"1892","127 - (1894) - And from Jabir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The people are followers of Quraysh in good and evil."
"1893","128 - (1895) - And from Jabir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Satan hears the call to prayer, he goes away until he is at the place of al-Rawha. Sulayman said: So I asked him about al-Rawha? He said: It is thirty-seven miles from Medina."
"1894","129 - (1896) - And from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse in Medina and it threw him onto a palm stump, so his foot was dislocated. We came to visit him and found him in a storeroom of Aishah glorifying Allah sitting, so we stood behind him and he was silent toward us. Then we came to him another time and found him praying the obligatory prayer, so we stood behind him and he signaled to us, so we sat. When he finished the prayer he said: When the imam prays sitting, then pray sitting, and when he prays standing, then pray standing, and do not do as the people of Persia do with their chiefs."
"1895","130 - (1897) - And from Jabir who said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we circumambulated the House and released ihram. When we came to al-Batha he ordered us to enter ihram for Hajj. Some of the people said: Shall we enter ihram for Hajj when our contact with women was only yesterday? There was some talk among them about that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I had known they would do this, I would not have brought the sacrificial animals. And he said to us: Let a group share in the sacrificial animal."
"1896","131 - (1898) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: We came from Mecca to Medina with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). My camel became exhausted and I stayed behind driving it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was behind attending to a need, so he caught up with me and said to me: Why are you behind? I said: Nothing, O Messenger of Allah, except that my camel went lame on me and I wanted to catch up with the people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took its tail and struck it, then urged it on, and said: Ride. Afterwards I found myself holding it back from the people. We stopped at a lodging before Medina, and I wanted to hurry to my family, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do not come to your family at night. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am newly married. He said: Whom did you marry? I said: A thayyib woman. He said: Why not a virgin whom you play with and she plays with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah died or was martyred and left young girls, so I disliked marrying someone like them to them. He was silent and did not say to me: You did well or you did badly. Then he said to me: Sell me this camel of yours. I said: No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No, rather sell it to me. I said: No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No, rather sell it to me. I said: A man owes me an ounce of gold, so it is yours for that. He said: I have taken it, so ride it to Medina. When I came to Medina, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Bilal: Give him an ounce of gold and add to it. So he gave me an ounce of gold and added a qirat to me. I said: The addition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will never leave me. It was in a bag of mine, then the people of Sham took it on the day of al-Harrah."
"1897","132 - (1899) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the son of Adam had palm trees, he would wish for the like of them besides, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."
"1898","133 - (1900) - And from Jabir: A slave boy of Hatib came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Hatib has entered the Fire. He said: You have lied; did he not witness Badr and al-Hudaybiyah?"
"1899","134 - (1901) - And from Jabir, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every servant will be resurrected upon what he died upon."
"1900","135 - (1902) - And from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of one man suffices two men, and the food of two men suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."
"1901","136 - (1903) - And from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for you do not know in which of them the blessing descends."
"1902","137 - (1904) - And from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Satan attends one of you at everything, until he attends him at his food and drink. So when a morsel of one of you falls, let him pick it up and remove what touched it of harm, then eat it and not leave it for Satan."
"1903","138 - (1905) - And from Jabir, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fears not waking at the end of the night, let him pray witr at the beginning of the night, then sleep. And whoever hopes to wake at the end of the night, let him pray witr at the end of the night, for the recitation is attended at the end of the night, and that is better."
"1904","139 - (1906) - And from Jabir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The people of Paradise eat and drink therein, and do not spit, nor urinate, nor blow their noses, nor defecate. He said: Then what becomes of the food? He said: Belching and sweat like the sweat of musk; they are inspired with glorification and praise as you are inspired with breath."
"1905","140 - (1907) - And from Jabir, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say three days before his death: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1906","141 - (1908) - And from Jabir who said: We did not pledge to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Hudaybiyah upon death, but we pledged to him not to flee, except Jadd ibn Qays who hid in the armpit of his camel."
"1907","142 - (1909) - And from Jabir, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The throne of Iblis is upon the sea, and he sends his troops to tempt people, and the greatest of them in his sight is the greatest of them in temptation."
"1908","143 - (1910) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir: A man of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a slave girl and I practice withdrawal from her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is decreed for her will come to her. Then he came to him afterwards and said: O Messenger of Allah, the slave girl has become pregnant. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No soul decreed by Allah to emerge except that it will come to be."
"1909","144 - (1911) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is in the night an hour which no Muslim man meets asking Allah for good of this world and the Hereafter except that He gives it to him."
"1910","145 - (1912) - And from Jabir who said: There was with the Mother of the Believers Aishah a woman with a boy whose nostrils dripped blood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: What is the matter with this boy? She said: He has udhrah. He said: Woe to you, O assembly of women, do not kill your children. Whatever woman has a boy with udhrah or pain in his head, let her take Indian costus and grind it, then administer it as nasal drops. Then he ordered Aishah, and she did that to the boy, and he recovered."
"1911","146 - (1913) - And from Jabir who said: A maternal uncle of mine of the Ansar used to perform ruqyah for snakebite, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ruqyah. So my uncle came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you forbade ruqyah, yet I perform ruqyah for snakebite. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Present it to me. So he presented it to him. He said: There is no harm in this; this is from the covenants."
"1912","147 - (1914) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: A man of the Ansar used to perform ruqyah for scorpion sting, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ruqyah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you forbade ruqyah, yet I used to perform ruqyah for scorpion sting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"1913","148 - (1915) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir who said: A boy was born to a man of us and he named him Muhammad. His people said to him: We will not let you name him with the name of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he went with his son carrying him on his back and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a boy was born to me and I named him Muhammad, but my people said to me: We will not let you name him with the name of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Name with my name, but do not use my kunyah, for I am only a Qasim dividing among you."
"1914","149 - (1916) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: I used to pray Dhuhr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I would take a handful of pebbles and put it in my palm, then move it to the other palm until it cooled, then place it for my forehead to prostrate on, due to the severe heat."
"1915","150 - (1917) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: We did not kill the traders of the polytheists at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1916","151 - (1918) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade exception in a sale unless it is known."
"1917","152 - (1919) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the dog and the cat, except the trained."
"1918","153 - (1920) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us, six hundred men, with Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and we had nothing except a bag of dates. We divided it, and each man of us got five dates or seven dates. We ate until hunger reached us. We sucked their pits. When hunger reached us, we reached the seacoast, and there was a mound like a huge sand dune from which the water had receded. Some of us said: Shall we eat this when it is carrion? Abu Ubaydah said: You are fighters in the path of Allah, eat, there is no harm. So we ate from it and salted from it and provisioned. When we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we mentioned that to him. He said: There is no harm in it. Does any of you have anything of it to feed me? Some of us said to others: Yes, so we sent some of it to him."
"1919","154 - (1921) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Haram died or was martyred owing a debt. I sought the help of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against his creditors to reduce his debt. I asked them and they refused. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go and sort your dates into kinds: ajwah by itself, and Adhq Zayd by itself, in kinds, then send for me. I did so, then sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came and sat on its top or in its middle, then said: Measure for the people. So I measured for them until I fulfilled what was theirs, then my dates remained as if nothing had decreased from them."
"1920","155 - (1922) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no breathing soul on earth that will reach one hundred years."
"1921","156 - (1923) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name with my name but do not use my kunyah, for I was only made a Qasim dividing among you."
"1922","156 - (1923 repeated) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name with my name but do not use my kunyah, for I was only made a Qasim dividing among you."
"1923","157 - (1924) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hasan ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Jabir: We used to pray Friday with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and rest our water camels. Hasan said: So I said to Jafar: Which hour is that? He said: The decline of the sun."
"1924","158 - (1925) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Musab narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse without a waist wrapper. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not admit his wife into the bathhouse. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not eat at a table on which wine is drunk."
"1925","159 - (1926) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Jabir who said: The Arabs used to be led in the pouring forth by a man called Abu Sayyarah on a donkey. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj, Quraysh stopped at their stations, saying: We are the Hums. So he went out until he stood at Arafat. That is His saying: {Then pour forth from where the people pour forth}."
"1926","160 - (1927) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Usamah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge with Allah from knowledge that does not benefit."
"1927","161 - (1928) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"1928","162 - (1929) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Abu Bakr used to pray with the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people prayed with the prayer of Abu Bakr."
"1929","163 - (1930) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Sharik, from Ibn Aqil, from Jabir: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wants to fast, let him take suhur even with something."
"1930","164 - (1931) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh."
"1931","165 - (1932) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ata and Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold a mudabbar slave."
"1932","166 - (1933) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Shabbabah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"1933","167 - (1934) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih and Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finishes his food, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."
"1934","168 - (1935) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith is among the people of Hijaz, and harshness and hardness of hearts is toward the east, among Rabiah and Mudar."
"1935","169 - (1936) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Sulayman, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) equipped an army until midnight passed or it reached that, then he came out to us and said: The people have prayed and slept, while you await this prayer. You will remain in prayer as long as you await it."
"1936","170 - (1937) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you wake? He said: Well, better than a man who neither woke fasting nor visited a sick person."
"1937","171 - (1938) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: A bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Tell me about Umrah, is it obligatory? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but that you perform Umrah is better for you."
"1938","172 - (1939) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to his companions one night while they waited for Isha, and said: The people have prayed and slept while you await it. You are in prayer as long as you await it. Then he said: Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the old age of the old, I would have delayed this prayer to half the night."
"1939","173 - (1940) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: al-Numan ibn Qawqal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if I deem the lawful lawful, and the unlawful unlawful, and pray the obligatory prayers, shall I enter Paradise? He said: He said: Yes."
"1940","174 - (1941) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the five prayers is like a flowing abundant river at the door of one of you in which he bathes five times every day."
"1941","175 - (1942) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say three days before his death: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah."
"1942","176 - (1943) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finishes the prayer in his mosque, let him give his house a share of his prayer, for Allah will place good in his house from his prayer."
"1943","177 - (1944) - And with it, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram for Hajj."
"1944","178 - (1945) - Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Yazid al-Himyari, al-Mundhir narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man performing ablution while washing his leather socks, so he poked him with his hand and said: We were not commanded this. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) showed him, moving his hand from the front of the socks to the shin and separating his fingers once."
"1945","179 - (1946) - Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah [text breaks off here in source]."
"1946","179 - (1946) (m) - And from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon on Friday. He said to him: Did you pray before you came? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rakahs and be brief in them."
"1947","180 - (1947) - Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Zad han, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a calamity occurs, or a dark wind blows, upon you is takbir, for it dispels the black dust."
"1948","181 - (1948) - Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Nukri narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir who said: I asked Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman: Which of the Quran was revealed first? He said: O you wrapped up. I said: Or Read in the name of your Lord who created. He said: I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah which of the Quran was revealed first? He said: O you wrapped up. I said: Or Read in the name of your Lord who created. Jabir said: I only tell you what the Messenger of Allah narrated to us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I stayed in Hira for a month. When I finished my stay, I descended and entered the belly of the valley. He said: So I was called. I looked before me and behind me, and on my right and on my left, and saw no one. Then I was called again. I looked before me and behind me, and on my right and on my left, and saw no one. Then I looked to the sky, and there he was upon the Throne in the air - Mubashshir said: meaning Jibril - so I was frightened. I came to Khadijah and ordered them, and they wrapped me. Then Allah revealed: O you wrapped up, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your garments purify."
"1949","182 - (1949) - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, who said: I asked Abu Salamah: Which of the Quran was revealed first? He said: O you wrapped up. He said: So I said: I was told that the first surah revealed of the Quran was: Read in the name of your Lord who created. Abu Salamah said: I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah: Which of the Quran was revealed first? He said: O you wrapped up. So I said to him: I was told that the first surah revealed of the Quran was: Read in the name of your Lord who created. Jabir said: I only narrate to you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us. He said: I stayed in Hira. When I finished my stay, I entered the valley. I was called. I looked before me and behind me, and on my right and on my left, and saw nothing. Then I was called and looked above me, and there I was with him sitting upon a throne between heaven and earth. He said: So I was frightened of him. I went to Khadijah and said: Wrap me, so they wrapped me, and pour cold water upon me. Then was revealed to me: O you wrapped up, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify."
"1950","183 - (1950) - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Ibn Miqsam narrated to me, who said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a funeral passed by us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for it. When we went to carry it, it was the funeral of a Jewish woman. We said: O Messenger of Allah, it is the funeral of a Jewish woman. He said: Death is a fright, so when you see a funeral, stand."
"1951","184 - (1951) - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Suayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: On the day of Uhud the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the martyrs who were martyred that day and said: Shroud them in their blood, for I have witnessed over these. Two men and three were buried in one grave, and he asked: Which of them knew the Quran most? Then he put him first. Jabir said: So my father and my uncle were buried that day in one grave."
"1952","185 - (1952) - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"1953","186 - (1953) - Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing between the servant and his leaving faith except his leaving prayer."
"1954","187 - (1954) - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: We were with Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah in a detachment or army, and our provisions ran out. We saw a whale cast up by the sea and wanted to eat from it, but Abu Ubaydah forbade us, then said: We are messengers of the Messenger of Allah, and in the path of Allah, eat. So we ate from it. When we returned, we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: If you have anything of it with you, send it to us."
"1955","188 - (1955) - Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us with three hundred riders, our commander Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, to watch a caravan of Quraysh. We stayed on the coast half a month, and severe hunger struck us until we ate leaves. That army was called the Army of Leaves. Then the sea cast to us a creature called amber. We ate from it half a month until our bodies recovered, and oiled ourselves with its fat. Abu Ubaydah took a rib from its ribs and looked for the tallest camel in the army and loaded it upon it, and it passed beneath it."
"1956","189 - (1956) - Abu Uthman said, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah said to us, Abu al-Zubayr said, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a bag containing dates. When it ran out, we felt its loss. A man would bring something. He said: And we took out from its eyes such and such jars of fat. He said: When we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he asked us: Do you have anything of it with you?"
"1957","190 - (1957) - Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: A man of the Muhajirin kicked a man of the Ansar. The Ansari said: O Ansar, and the Muhajiri said: O Muhajirin. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that, he said: What is with the call of Jahiliyyah? They said: O Messenger of Allah, a man of the Muhajirin kicked a man of the Ansar. He said: Leave it, for it is foul. Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul said: Did they do it? If we return to Medina, the mightier will expel the humbler from it. Umar said: Let me, O Messenger of Allah, strike the neck of this hypocrite. He said: Leave him, lest people say Muhammad kills his companions."
"1958","191 - (1958) - Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Abdullah ibn Ubayy after he was put in his pit. He ordered him, so he was brought out and placed upon his knees. He blew upon him from his saliva and clothed him his shirt, and Allah knows best."
"1959","192 - (1959) - Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: A man of the Muhajirin kicked a man of the Ansar. The people of this one came, and the people of that one came. These said: O Muhajirin, and these said: O Ansar. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Leave it, for it is foul. Then he said: What is with the call of Jahiliyyah? What is with the call of Jahiliyyah?"
"1960","193 - (1960) - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver, its two witnesses, and its writer, and said: They are equal."
"1961","194 - (1961) - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid who said: Some of our shaykhs narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah that Abu Bakr said: Whoever had a promise from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him stand. He said: So I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised me to give me such and such, scooping with his hand three scoops. He said: So Abu Bakr said: When wealth comes to us, come to us. Wealth came to him, so I came to him. He said: So I scooped it with my hands. He said: Count it, and it was five hundred. He said: So he gave me another thousand. He said: And he said: Do you have other wealth? He said: I said: No. He said: When a year passes over it, pay its zakat."
"1962","195 - (1962) - Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, that Abu Bakr said: Whoever has a promise, let him stand. He mentioned similar except that he did not mention therein the saying of Abu Bakr: When a year passes, nor his saying: Do you have other wealth."
"1963","196 - (1963) - Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir who said: I ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman, bread and meat, then they prayed and did not perform ablution."
"1964","197 - (1964) - Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my minbar and my chamber is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon a rivulet from the rivulets of Paradise."
"1965","198 - (1965) - Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar informed us, from Abu Hubayrah al-Ansari, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought from me a camel of mine while we were on a journey. He gave me its back to ride until we arrive. When we arrived, I brought him the camel and handed it to him. He ordered for me its price: two ounces. I left, and his messenger followed me and said: Come, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you. I thought he had changed his mind. When I came to him, he said to me: Take your camel, it is yours. So I left, and met a Jewish man and told him of what happened. He marveled and said: He gave you the price and returned the camel to you?"
"1966","199 - (1966) - Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, Jabir heard, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When the wealth of Bahrayn comes, we will give you thus and thus. And Sufyan scooped with his hand three scoops."
"1967","200 - (1967) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: When was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say He is Able to send punishment upon you from above you, he said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or from beneath your feet, he said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or clothe you in parties and taste some of you the might of others, he said: These two are lighter, or these two are easier."
"1968","201 - (1968) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, Jabir narrated to us, the Prophet said: War is deceit. Abu Uthman said: Some of our companions told me: Many of them said: War is khadaa, but I only heard it with damma: khudaa."
"1969","202 - (1969) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: A man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon on Friday. He said: Did you pray? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rakahs."
"1970","203 - (1970) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon on Friday. He said: Did you pray? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rakahs."
"1971","204 - (1971) - Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, who said: I said to Amr: Did you hear Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: A man passed with arrows in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Hold their blades?"
"1972","205 - (1972) - Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: A man said on the day of Uhud: O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed, where am I? He said: In Paradise. So he threw dates in his hand and fought until he was killed."
"1973","206 - (1973) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, pointing to his ears: My ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That people will exit the Fire and enter Paradise."
"1974","207 - (1974) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, did you marry? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a thayyib? He said: I said: No, rather a thayyib. He said: Why not a young girl whom you play with and she plays with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was killed on the day of Uhud leaving nine daughters, and they are my nine sisters. I did not like to bring to them a foolish girl like them, but a woman to comb them and care for them. He said: You did right."
"1975","208 - (1975) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fed us horse meat, and forbade us donkey meat."
"1976","209 - (1976) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a house. I heard in it a noise. I said: Whose is this? They said: For a man of Quraysh. I said: Who is he? They said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. I wanted to enter it, but remembered your jealousy, O Abu Hafs. He wept and said: Would I be jealous toward you, O Messenger of Allah?!"
"1977","210 - (1977) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: A man freed a slave boy of his after his death, having no wealth besides him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold him, and Ibn al-Nahham bought him from him."
"1978","211 - (1978) - Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir ibn Abd Allah heard saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me when I married: Did you take patterned blankets? I said: How would we have patterned blankets? He said: They will come to be."
"1979","212 - (1979) - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, who said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad and Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon on Friday, a caravan came to Medina. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rushed to it until none remained with him except twelve men. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, if you followed until none of you remained, the valley would flow with Fire for you. Then this verse was revealed: And when they see trade or amusement, they disperse to it and leave you standing. And he said: Among the twelve who stood firm with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Abu Bakr and Umar."
"1980","213 - (1980) - Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Mahbub narrated to us, from Usamah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said upon the minbar: Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge with Allah from knowledge that does not benefit."
"1981","214 - (1981) - Abd Allah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu Talib al-Qass, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Excellent condiment is vinegar, and enough evil for a man to despise what is brought to him."
"1982","215 - (1982) - Ubayd Allah ibn Umar Abu Said narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Amr informed us, from Jabir who said: When was revealed: Say He is Able to send punishment upon you from above you or from beneath your feet, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or clothe you in parties and taste some of you the might of others, he said: This is lighter, or this is easier."
"1983","216 - (1983) - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: When was revealed: He is Able to send punishment upon you from above you, he said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or from beneath your feet, he said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or clothe you in parties, he said: This is lighter."
"1984","217 - (1984) - Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, that a man of the Ansar freed a slave boy of his, having no wealth besides him. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Who will buy him from me? Nuaym ibn Abd Allah bought him for eight hundred and handed it to him. He said: I heard Jabir say: A Coptic slave who died the year before."
"1985","218 - (1985) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, with its isnad, similar."
"1986","219 - (1986) - Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that a man of the Muhajirin kicked a man of the Ansar. The people of this one and the people of that one gathered. This one said: O Muhajirin, and this one said: O Ansar. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Leave it, for it is foul. Then he said: What is with the call of Jahiliyyah? What is with the call of Jahiliyyah?"
"1987","220 - (1987) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, with its isnad, similar."
"1988","221 - (1988) - Ubayd Allah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir: That a man entered while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon on Friday. He said: Did you pray, O so-and-so? He said: No. He said: Then stand and bow."
"1989","222 - (1989) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered the sermon to the people on Friday, he mentioned similar."
"1990","223 - (1990) - al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: My father died leaving seven daughters or nine daughters - Hammad said: I only know he said: nine - so I married a thayyib woman. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Did you marry, O Jabir? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a thayyib? I said: A thayyib. He said: Why not a young girl whom you play with and she plays with you, or he said: you laugh with and she laughs with you? He said: I said: Abdullah died leaving nine daughters, and I disliked bringing to them one like them. I wanted a woman to care for them. He said to me: May Allah bless you, or he said good."
"1991","224 - (1991) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, I heard Jabir saying: My father died leaving nine - or seven - so he mentioned similar, except that he said: So he said to me: May Allah bless you, and he supplicated for me."
"1992","225 - (1992) - Ubayd Allah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, who said: I said to Amr ibn Dinar: O Abu Muhammad, did you hear Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Allah brings people out of the Fire by intercession? He said: Yes."
"1993","226 - (1993) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us with its isnad similar."
"1994","227 - (1994) - Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Jabir: That a man passed with arrows in the mosque with their blades exposed. He was ordered to hold their blades lest he scratch a Muslim."
"1995","228 - (1994 [m]) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, similar."
"1996","229 - (1995) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, who said: I said to Amr: Did you hear Jabir narrate that a man entered the mosque with arrows, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take their blades? He said: Yes."
"1997","230 - (1996) - Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir - Hammad said: I only know he raised it - that he forbade leasing land."
"1998","231 - (1997) - Abu Said al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Matar, from Ata, from Jabir, raising it, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leasing land."
"1999","232 - (1998) - Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and permitted the meat of horses."
"2000","233 - (1999) - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit that Jabir ibn Abd Allah told him, he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Kab ibn Ujrah: O Kab ibn Ujrah, prayer is nearness, and fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire. O Kab ibn Ujrah, people are two morning-goers: a seller of himself destroying his neck, and a buyer of himself freeing his neck."
"2001","234 - (2000) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, Jabir heard saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When a slave marries without the permission of his master, he is a fornicator."
"2002","235 - (2001) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked anything and said: No."
"2003","236 - (2002) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Muhammad al-Sulami narrated to us - Sufyan said: I think he is the son of Ali, cousin of al-Mansur - from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, Jabir heard saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, did you know that Allah gave life to your father and said to him: Wish upon Allah. He said: Return me to the world to be killed again. He said: I decreed that they do not return."
"2004","237 - (2003) - Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: When the sea emigrants returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Will you not tell of the wonders you saw in the land of Abyssinia? Youths of them said: O Messenger of Allah, while we sat, an old woman of their old women passed carrying upon her head a water jar. She passed a youth of them, who put one of his hands between her shoulders and pushed her. She fell upon her knees and her jar broke. When she rose, she turned to him and said: You will know, O traitor, when Allah sets the Throne, and gathers the first and the last, and hands and feet speak of what they earned, you will know how my affair and your affair with Him is tomorrow. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: She spoke truth, she spoke truth. How does Allah sanctify a people among whom the right of their weak is not taken from their strong."
"2005","238 - (2004) - Ishaq narrated to us, Malik ibn Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: During the Trench, I looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him placing a stone between him and his waist to straighten his back from hunger."
"2006","239 - (2005) - Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih and Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: A man called Abu Humayd came with a cup of milk from al-Naqi. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not cover it, even with a stick placed across it."
"2007","240 - (2006) - Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: A man used to perform ruqyah for scorpion sting, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ruqyah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you forbade ruqyah yet I used to perform ruqyah for scorpion sting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"2008","241 - (2007) - Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: My maternal uncle of the Ansar used to perform ruqyah for venom. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Present it to me. So he presented it to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm in this; this is from the covenants."
"2009","242 - (2008) - Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced, and not spread his forearms like the dog spreads."
"2010","243 - (2009) - Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: There was with Aishah a woman. Abu Yala said: pouring over a boy whose nostrils dripped blood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: What is the matter with this boy? They said: He has udhrah. He said: Woe to you, O assembly of women, do not kill your children. Whatever woman has a boy with udhrah or pain in his head, let her take Indian costus and grind it, then administer nasal drops. Then he ordered Aishah, and she did that to the boy, and he recovered."
"2011","244 - (2010) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated kept apart until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"2012","245 - (2011) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that the delegation of Thaqif asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): They said: Our land is a cold land, so how with ghusl? He said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"2013","246 - (2012) - Ishaq narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: Neither the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor his companions circumambulated between Safa and Marwa except one tawaf: his first tawaf."
"2014","247 - (2013) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Suayr, from Jabir who said: On the day of Uhud the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the martyrs who were martyred that day, and said: Shroud them in their blood, for I have witnessed over these. Two men and three were buried in one grave, and he asked which of them knew the Quran most, then put him first. Jabir said: So my father and my uncle were buried that day in one grave."
"2015","248 - (2014) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, heard it from Jabir, and Amr ibn Dinar, Jabir ibn Abd Allah heard saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a house, or a palace. I heard in it a voice, or a noise. I said: Whose is this? It was said: It is for Ibn al-Khattab. Sufyan said: Ibn al-Munkadir added: I wanted to enter it, but remembered your jealousy. Umar wept. He said: O Prophet of Allah, would I be jealous toward you?"
"2016","249 - (2015) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir ibn Abd Allah heard, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, did you take patterned blankets? I said: O Messenger of Allah, how would we have patterned blankets. He said: They will come to be."
"2017","250 - (2016) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir ibn Abd Allah heard saying: A boy was born to a man of us and he named him al-Qasim. We said: We will not kunya you Abu al-Qasim, nor please your eye. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Name him Abd al-Rahman."
"2018","251 - (2017) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat then prayed without performing ablution, and that Abu Bakr ate meat then prayed without performing ablution, and that Umar ibn al-Khattab ate meat then prayed without performing ablution."
"2019","252 - (2018) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, heard from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: I fell sick, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr came to me walking. They found me unconscious. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and poured his ablution water upon me. I woke. I asked him: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how do I dispose of my wealth? He did not answer me, until the inheritance verse was revealed, meaning His saying: Allah instructs you concerning your children."
"2020","253 - (2019) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If the wealth of Bahrayn comes, I will give you thus and thus and thus. And Sufyan scooped, showing us with his hand three scoops toward his head. The wealth of Bahrayn did not come until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away. When the wealth of Bahrayn came, Abu Bakr stood and said: Whoever had a promise or debt upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him come. Jabir said: So I came to him and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised me. He said: So he gave me. Then I came to him after that asking him, and he did not give me. Then I came to him a third time and said: I asked you and you did not give me, and I asked and you did not give me. Either give, or be miserly to me. He said: What disease is worse than miserliness! I did not withhold from you once except while wanting to give you."
"2021","254 - (2020) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir, similar, except that he said: He scooped for me a scoop. I counted it and found it five hundred. He said: So he said: Take like it twice."
"2022","255 - (2021) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir heard saying: My father was killed on the day of Uhud. He was brought mutilated, and placed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I wanted to uncover him, but my people forbade me twice. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him lifted. Sufyan said: As if they were returned to their death places. He said: He heard the voice of a wailing woman. He said: Who is this? They said: The daughter of Amr or the sister of Amr. He said: Why does she weep? Or do not weep, for the angels kept shading him with their wings until he was lifted."
"2023","256 - (2022) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir heard saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people on the day of the Trench, and al-Zubayr volunteered. Then he called the people, and al-Zubayr volunteered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a hawari, and my hawari is al-Zubayr."
"2024","257 - (2023) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir heard saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Medina is like the bellows, expelling its filth, and its good becomes pure."
"2025","258 - (2024) - Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir heard saying: The Jews said: Whoever comes his wife in her front from behind, the child will be cross-eyed. Then was revealed: Your women are tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish."
"2026","259 - (2025) - Ishaq narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm in animals, two for one, hand to hand, but no good in it on credit."
"2027","260 - (2026) - Ishaq and Zuhayr narrated to us, both said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man with dirty clothes and said: Did this one find nothing to clean his clothes? And he saw a man with disheveled hair and said: Did this one find nothing to calm his hair?"
"2028","261 - (2027) - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed nine years in Medina without performing Hajj, then announced departure among the people. When he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, he prayed at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr. She sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Bathe, wrap with a cloth, and enter ihram. She said: So she did. When the chest of the camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) settled upon the back of al-Bayda, he entered ihram. We entered ihram knowing it only as Hajj, and for it we went out. The Messenger of Allah was among us, the Quran descended upon him, he knew its interpretation, and he only did what he was commanded. Jabir said: So I looked before me, behind me, on my right, on my left, as far as my sight, the people walkers and riders. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to say talbiyah: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wal-nimata laka wal-mulk, la sharika lak. When we came to Mecca, he began and touched the Corner, then ran three circuits and walked four. When he finished his tawaf, he went to the Maqam and said: Allah said: And take the Maqam of Ibrahim as a prayer place. So he prayed behind the Maqam of Ibrahim two rakahs. Jafar said: My father said: He recited in them with Tawhid: Say O disbelievers, and Say He is Allah, One. He said: And he did not mention that from Jabir. Then he went to the Corner and touched it, then went to Safa. He said: We begin with what Allah began with: Indeed Safa and Marwa are from the rites of Allah. He ascended Safa until the House appeared to him. He magnified three times and said: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him. His is dominion and praise. He gives life and death. In His hand is good, and He is over all things Capable, three times. Then he supplicated therein. Then he descended from Safa and walked until when his feet poured in the belly of the valley, he ran, until when his feet ascended from the belly of the valley, he walked to Marwa. He ascended Marwa until the House appeared to him, and said like what he said upon Safa. He circumambulated seven. He said: Whoever has no sacrificial animal with him, let him release ihram. Whoever has sacrificial with him, let him remain upon his ihram. For were it not that my sacrificial is with me, I would release. Had I faced of my affair what I now know, I would enter umrah. Ali came from Yemen. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With what did you enter ihram, O Ali? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger enters. He said: I have sacrificial with me, so do not release. Ali said: So I entered upon Fatimah, and she had applied kohl and worn dyed clothes. I said: Who ordered you with this? She said: My father ordered me. Ali used to say in Iraq: So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inciting against Fatimah, seeking confirmation in what she said. He said: She spoke truth, I ordered her. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed one hundred camels, of that with his hand sixty-three, and Ali sacrificed what remained. Then he took from each camel a piece and cooked them together. They ate of the meat and drank of the broth. Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for our year or forever? He said: No, rather forever. Umrah entered into Hajj, and he interlaced between his fingers."
"2029","262 - (2028) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: We came to Jabir ibn Abd Allah, then he mentioned similar."
"2030","263 - (2029) - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Nadr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Amr say: al-Hajjaj came and delayed the prayer. We asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah about that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr at midday when the sun declines, and Asr while the sun is clear, and Maghrib when the sun sets, and Isha sometimes delayed and sometimes hastened. When he saw the people gathered, he hastened. When he saw them delayed, he delayed. And they - or he - prayed Fajr in darkness."
"2031","Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever does not give up mukhabarah (leasing land for a share of produce), let him take notice of war from Allah and His Messenger."
"2032","Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I heard Mutamir say: My father narrated, from Khidash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you lies on his back, let him not place one of his feet over the other."
"2033","Zakariyya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he made the two sons of Suriya swear when he asked them about stoning, so he made them swear: how do you find it in the Book of Allah, in your book? He made them swear by Allah, besides Whom there is no god, Who revealed the Torah to Musa: how do you find the hadd of the adulterer in your book?"
"2034","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abdulmalik narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir who said: I attended the Eid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he prayed before delivering the sermon, without adhan or iqamah, then he delivered the sermon after praying, admonished the people and reminded them, then he came to the women and admonished them, and Bilal was with him, and he reminded them and commanded them to give charity. He said: So the woman began to throw her ring, her earring, and things like that, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal and he gathered what was there. Then he said: Indeed only a few of you will be in Paradise. A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, why? He said: You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands."
"2035","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abdulmalik who said: I heard Ata narrating from Jabir who said: We used to perform tamattu with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we would slaughter a cow on behalf of seven, sharing in it."
"2036","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it; if he is unable, let him grant it to his Muslim brother, and let him not lease it for rent."
"2037","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abd Rabbih ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For every disease there is a remedy; when the remedy of the disease is applied, he recovers by the permission of Allah."
"2038","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr narrated to him that Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to him that Jabir ibn Abdullah visited al-Muqanna, then said: I will not leave until you get cupped, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed in it there is healing."
"2039","Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that from every harvest of dates, ten wasqs be set aside as a bunch hung in the mosque for the poor."
"2040","Abu Hammam narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb informed me, saying: Dawud ibn Qays al-Madani and others informed me, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the wife of Sad ibn al-Rabi said: O Messenger of Allah, Sad has died leaving two daughters, his brother, and his brother seized what Sad left, and women are married for their wealth. He did not answer her in that sitting. Then she came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the two daughters of Sad. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call his brother to me. He came, and he said: Give his two daughters two-thirds, his wife one-eighth, and what remains is yours."
"2041","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Miswar ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Every good deed is charity, and whatever a man spends on his family and wealth is recorded for him as charity, and whatever he protects his honour with is charity for him. He said: And every spending of a believer, except in disobedience, Allah guarantees its recompense, except his spending on buildings. Miswar said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir said: So we said to Jabir ibn Abdullah: What did he mean by his words: what a man protects his honour with? He said: He gives to the poet and the foul-tongued person. Jabir said: As if he means: the one whose tongue is feared."
"2042","Abu Ali al-Shaylamani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ismail al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any youth who marries in his early age, his devil cries out: Woe to him, woe to him, he has protected his religion from me."
"2043","Al-Shaylamani narrated to us with this chain, from Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: If only one day remained of my life, I would meet Allah with a wife, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The worst of you are your unmarried ones."
"2044","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Abdullah al-Umari narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Ata narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when a large bowl is brought to you in the morning and another in the evening? They said: O Messenger of Allah, on that day we will be in good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather, you today are better."
"2045","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Describe the lineage of Allah. So Allah revealed: Say: He is Allah, the One, to its end."
"2046","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, Abdul Majid ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the most beloved food to Allah is that over which many hands gather."
"2047","Abu al-Harith Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Will we weave our garments in Paradise with our own hands? The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed. The Bedouin said: Why do you laugh at an ignorant man asking a learned man? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have spoken the truth, O Bedouin, but they are fruits (that emerge)."
"2048","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Abu Talib, whether his prophethood would benefit him. He said: Yes, I have brought him out from the depth of Hell to its shallow edge. And he was asked about Khadijah, because she died before the obligations and the rulings of the Quran; he said: I saw her by a river of the rivers of Paradise, in a house of pearl with no noise in it and no hardship. And he was asked about Waraqah ibn Nawfal; he said: I saw him in the midst of Paradise wearing silk brocade. And he was asked about Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl; he said: He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone, between me and Isa, peace be upon them."
"2049","Al-Hasan ibn Isa ibn Masarjis, freedman of Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the sun had declined."
"2050","Abdul Ghaffar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Sad ibn Abi Waqqas came forward. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is my maternal uncle."
"2051","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, al-Nadr informed us, Abu al-Awwam Abdul Aziz ibn Rabi al-Bahili informed us, whose house was in the dwelling of Ziyad, saying: I heard Abu al-Zubayr, whose name is Muhammad, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he came upon two graves whose occupants were being punished. He said: They are not being punished for something major: one of them used to backbite people, and the other did not guard himself from his urine. He called for a moist palm stalk, or two stalks, and broke them, then ordered each piece to be planted over a grave. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will lighten their punishment as long as they remain moist, or until they dry."
"2052","Shayban narrated to us, Talhah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubaydah ibn Hassan, from Ata al-Kaykharani, from Jabir who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a house among a group of Muhajirun including Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each man stand up to his counterpart. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to Uthman and embraced him, saying: You are my ally in this world, and you are my ally in the Hereafter."
"2053","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The people of Paradise eat and drink therein, and do not spit, urinate, blow their noses, or defecate. He said: So what happens to the food? He said: Belching and sweat like the sweat of musk; they are inspired with tasbih and tahmid just as you are inspired with breath."
"2054","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say three days before his death: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah."
"2055","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act for a matter already decreed or for a matter we are just beginning? He said: For a matter already decreed. Suraqah ibn Malik said: Then what is the point of action? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each is facilitated toward his deed."
"2056","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir ibn Dirham al-Anbari narrated to us, Abdul Aziz ibn Rabi al-Bahili narrated to us, from Ata ibn Rabah, from Jabir who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he came upon two graves being punished. He said: They are being punished for nothing major: backbiting and urine. Then he called for a palm stalk, broke it, placed a piece over each of them, and said: I hope it will lighten them as long as they do not dry."
"2057","Al-Jarrah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Khurasani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhriz al-Azdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That the belly of one of you be filled with pus or blood is better for him than being filled with poetry by which I was satirized."
"2058","Abdul Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Abu Taybah and he cupped him; he asked him: What is your fee? He said: Three sa. So he reduced a sa from him."
"2059","Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Mahmud ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid at bedtime, for it clears the vision and grows hair."
"2060","Al-Fadl ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Said ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Greeting comes before speech."
"2061","And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, in a repeated narration: And do not invite anyone to food until he gives salam."
"2062","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, al-Wazi ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir who said: We were praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of Badr when he smiled in his prayer. When he finished the prayer, we said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you smiling? He said: Mikail passed by me, with a trace of dust on his wing, returning from pursuing the people; he laughed to me, so I smiled to him."
"2063","Amr narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, Harun ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"2064","Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, known as Ibn al-Shair, narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picking kabath fruit. He said: Take the black of it, for it is the tastiest. We said: Did you used to herd sheep? He said: Yes, and is there any prophet who did not herd them?"
"2065","Salih ibn Malik narrated to us, Abdul Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown that I entered Paradise, and there I was with al-Rumaysa, wife of Abu Talhah. He said: And I heard a light footstep before me, so I said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Bilal. He said: And I saw a white palace with a slave girl in its courtyard. I said: Whose palace is this? She said: It belongs to Umar ibn al-Khattab. I wanted to enter it to look at it, but I remembered your jealousy, O Umar. Umar said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, would I be jealous with regard to you?"
"2066","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mukhabarah."
"2067","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Karib, from Jabir: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"2068","Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, from Abu al-Awwam, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two graves and said: They are being punished, and they are not being punished for something major: one of them did not guard himself from his urine, and the other used to backbite people."
"2069","Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"2070","Qasim narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"2071","Qasim narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"2072","Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"2073","Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, Matar narrated to us, from Talhah, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims someone other than his father, or affiliates himself with other than his masters out of aversion to them, upon him is the curse of Allah; whoever curses his parents likewise; whoever dedicates a sacrifice to other than Allah likewise; whoever violates anything of the sanctity of Makkah likewise; and whoever says about me what I did not say likewise."
"2074","Jafar ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of the dogs of Madinah. Ibn Umm Maktum came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind, my house is far, and I have a dog. He permitted him for some days, then ordered his dog to be killed, and it was killed."
"2075","Jafar ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir who said: Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind, my house is far, and I hear the adhan. He said: If you hear the adhan, answer it, even crawling or dragging yourself."
"2076","Jafar ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir who said: A man used to carry wine from Khaybar to Madinah and sell it to the Muslims; he carried a load of it worth money and arrived with it in Madinah. A Muslim man met him and said: O so-and-so, wine has been prohibited. So he placed it where he stopped, on a mound, and covered it with garments, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have heard that wine has been prohibited? He said: Yes. He said: May I return it to the one I bought it from? He said: Returning it is not lawful. He said: May I gift it? ... and he mentioned the hadith."
"2077","Jafar narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, from Husayn ibn Harmalah, from Abu al-Musabbih, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant's feet become dusty for an hour of the day in the path of Allah but they are forbidden to the Fire."
"2078","Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Said ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Iyad, from Jabir who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a slave girl, and I practice coitus interruptus with her. He said: That will not prevent anything Allah has decreed. It was not long before he came and said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): She has become pregnant. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger."
"2079","Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir, that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate for me and for my husband. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you and your husband."
"2080","Hafs al-Hulwani narrated to us, Buhlul ibn Muwarriq al-Shami narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from his brother, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation will remain dominant upon the truth until Isa son of Maryam descends; their imam will say: Come forward. He will say: You are more entitled; some of you are leaders over others, an honour by which Allah has honoured this nation."
"2081","Ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, saying: My father said, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: My father ordered khazirah, and it was prepared; then he ordered me and I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I came to him while he was at his house. He said: He said to me: What is with you, O Jabir, is it meat? He said: I said: No. He said: I came to my father, and he said to me: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. He said: Did you hear him say anything? He said: I said: Yes, he said to me: What is with you, O Jabir, is it meat? He said: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a craving, so he ordered a domestic sheep of ours, and it was slaughtered, then ordered it roasted, then ordered me and I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to me: What is with you, O Jabir? I informed him, and he said: May Allah reward the Ansar well on our behalf, especially Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Haram and Sad ibn Ubadah."
"2082","Ahmad ibn al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, saying: My father said, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: My father ordered harirah and it was prepared; then he ordered me and I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned something similar."
"2083","Harun narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, conveying from the Prophet: The best jihad is one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed."
"2084","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people on the day of the Trench: who will bring him news of Banu Qurayzah? Al-Zubayr volunteered, then he called them again and al-Zubayr volunteered, three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"2085","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr who said: Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm al-Saib, or Umm al-Musayyib, while she was shivering. He said: What is wrong with you, O Umm al-Saib, or O Umm al-Musayyib, that you are shivering? She said: Fever, may Allah not bless it. He said: Do not curse fever, for it removes the sins of the son of Adam just as the bellows removes the dross of iron."
"2086","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Jabir who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came with an egg-sized piece of gold he had found in one of the campaigns. He said: He stood it on his left side and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, take this from me as charity, for by Allah I own no wealth besides it. He turned away from him. Then he came to him from his right side and said the same to him, and he turned away. Then he came to him from in front and said the same, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said angrily: Bring it. He said: When he gave it to him, he threw it at him; had it hit him it would have hurt or wounded him. Then he said: One of you comes with his wealth, owning nothing besides it, giving it in charity, then sits afterwards begging people? Charity is only from surplus wealth. Take your wealth from us; we have no need of it."
"2087","Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, al-Muafa narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Ata, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good deed one of you does for a rich or poor person is charity for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"2088","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us istikhara as he used to teach us ... and he mentioned the hadith."
"2089","Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Umar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that a cow turned over some wine and drank it, and they feared for it, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Eat it; there is no harm in eating it."
"2090","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Sharik, from Ibn Aqil, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends to fast, let him take suhur, even with something small."
"2091","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, al-Furat ibn Abi al-Furat al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I slept then woke, then slept then woke. A Muslim man stood and said: Prayer, prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with his head dripping, led us in prayer, then said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would love that they pray this prayer at this hour. Al-Furat said: I think it was Isha."
"2092","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days better to Allah than the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. He said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, are they better, or their equivalent in jihad in the path of Allah? He said: They are better than their equivalent in jihad in the path of Allah, except one who rubs his face in the dust. And there is no day better to Allah than the day of Arafah: Allah descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of the people of the earth to the people of heaven, saying: Look at My servants, disheveled, dusty, exposed to the sun, coming from every deep mountain pass; they have not seen My mercy, nor seen My punishment. I have never seen a day with more freed from the Fire than the day of Arafah."
"2093","Hajjaj ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah who said: I heard Jabir narrating that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Quraysh disbelieved me at the time I was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis, I stood in the Hijr and Allah displayed Bayt al-Maqdis to me, and I began informing them of its signs while looking at it."
"2094","Hajjaj narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is given an umra gift for himself and his descendants, it belongs to him outright; the giver may impose no condition or exception in it."
"2095","Hajjaj narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed: If a man grants another an umra for himself and his descendants, saying: I give it to you and your descendants as long as any of you remains, then it belongs to the one given it, and it does not return to its owner, because he gave a gift in which inheritance applies."
"2096","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women are married only to suitable matches, and only guardians marry them off, and there is no dowry less than ten dirhams."
"2097","Abu Basit narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, from Maiz al-Tamimi, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but he seeks to stir discord among them."
"2098","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Khattab al-Basri narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in a hadith of his: When the Arabs are humiliated, Islam is humiliated."
"2099","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a man of his companions entered upon an Ansari man while he was diverting water in his garden. He said: If you have water that spent this night in a skin, otherwise we will drink directly? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I have water that spent the night in a skin. He said: We went to the shelter; he went and milked a sheep over water that had spent the night in a skin. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, then the same was repeated and his companion drank."
"2100","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, saying: I asked Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir about ablution after what fire has touched. He said: Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to me, saying: I ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed without performing ablution after his first ablution. Then I ate with Abu Bakr and he prayed without ablution; then I ate with Umar and he prayed without ablution; then I ate with Uthman and he prayed without ablution."
"2101","Ghassan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a donkey branded on its face. He said: Did I not forbid this? May Allah curse whoever does it; and he forbade striking the face."
"2102","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir al-Ghasil narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Jabir who said: He came visiting al-Muqanna ibn Sinan, who was the maternal uncle of Asim, his mothers brother; he greeted him while he was in a cloak and waist-wrapper, his sight afflicted, with some yellow dye on his head and beard. He said: What do you complain of? He said: A boil that prevents me sleeping and keeps me awake. Jabir said: O boy, call us a cupper. Al-Muqanna said: What will you do with a cupper, O Abu Abdullah? He said: I want to apply a cupping glass to it. He said: May Allah forgive you; even a garment touching me, or a fly landing on me, hurts me. When he saw his distress at that, he began narrating to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is any good in your remedies, it is in a cupping incision, a drink of honey, or a cauterization matching the ailment; and I do not like to be cauterized. He called the cupper and applied the cupping glass to his boil; when it reached the lower edge of his eyebrow, he incised it with a lancet he had, and Allah removed what was in it of harm, and he was cured."
"2103","Abdul Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Sad ibn Abi Waqqas came forward. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is my maternal uncle."
"2104","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between a servant and disbelief is abandoning prayer."
"2105","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr who said: When al-Hajjaj arrived he began delaying prayer, so I asked Jabir - or he was asked - and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr at midday heat, pray Asr while the sun was still bright, pray Maghrib when the sun had set, and Isha: when people gathered he hastened it, when people were few he delayed it; and he prayed Fajr in darkness."
"2106","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: I used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return to my family in Banu Salimah, a mile from Madinah, or he said: from the mosque, while I could still see where arrows landed. Then he said: Zuhr is as its name, at midday; Asr while the sun is white and clear; Maghrib as its name; Isha: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes delay it and sometimes hasten it."
"2107","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying in a single garment wrapped around him. Abu al-Zubayr said: I saw Jabir praying in a single garment wrapped around him."
"2108","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you fears not waking at the end of the night, let him perform witr at the beginning of the night; and whoever hopes to wake at the end of the night, let him perform witr at the end of the night, for prayer at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."
"2109","Ammar Abu Yasir narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, al-Jad informed us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The people complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day of thirst. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a large cup, saying: Does any of you have water? He said: A small water-skin was brought, and he poured it in. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand in the cup. Jabir said: I was looking at springs gushing between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the people drew water."
"2110","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the jamrah with pebbles like those used for flinging."
"2111","Abu Hammam narrated to us, saying: al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab narrated to me, Maqil ibn Ubaydullah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guarantees me what is between his jaws and his legs, I guarantee him Paradise."
"2112","Abu Hammam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to me, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act for a matter already decreed or for a matter we are just beginning? He said: For a matter already decreed. Suraqah said: Then what is the point of action? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each is facilitated toward his deed."
"2113","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon, his eyes reddened, his voice rose, and his anger intensified, as if he were warning of an army, saying: It will attack you morning and evening. And he would say: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two - joining the index and middle fingers - and say: To proceed: the best speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the worst matters are invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance. Then he would say: I am closer to every believer than his own self; whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family; whoever leaves debt or dependents, it is to me and upon me."
"2114","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ashath, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Bakrah: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon on the day of sacrifice on his mount at Mina."
"2115","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan and Abu Salih, or one of them, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of sacrifice at Mina, similar to the hadith of Abu Bakrah."
"2116","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the earnings of the cupper. He said: I think he said: Feed it to your water-carrying camel."
"2117","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: We did not call the hypocrites disbelievers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2118","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Habib al-Muallim, from Ata, from Jabir, that a man said on the day of the Conquest: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah grants you victory, I would pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray here. The man repeated it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twice or three times, each time he said: Pray here. When he persisted, he said: Then do as you wish."
"2119","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him pray two rakahs before sitting."
"2120","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that when the death of the Negus reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he stood with his companions, they lined up behind him in two rows, and he prayed over him."
"2121","Ibrahim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon, his eyes reddened, his anger intensified, and his voice rose, as if he were warning of an army. Then he said: The Hour has come upon you morning and evening; I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two: the index and middle fingers. To proceed: the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, the worst matters are invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance."
"2122","Ibrahim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on his mount facing whatever direction in the campaign of Anmar."
"2123","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deception."
"2124","Ishaq narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that they would not put their hands in food until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began."
"2125","Ishaq narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar and Mughirah informed us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir who said: I sold the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a camel, on condition that I keep its use until I return to Madinah."
"2126","Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir: that he sold the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a camel, stipulating its use for himself until reaching his family."
"2127","Ishaq narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar informed us, from Abu Hubayrah, from Jabir who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he bought a camel from me, granting me its use until I reach Madinah. When we arrived, I brought the camel to him and handed it over, and he ordered the price for me. Then I left, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught up with me. He said: I said: Perhaps he changed his mind about it. He said: When I came to him, he handed the camel to me, saying: It is yours. He said: I passed by a Jewish man and informed him. He said: He was amazed. He said: He bought the camel from you, paid you the price, then gifted it to you? He said: I said: Yes."
"2128","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father who said: We came to Jabir ibn Abdullah while he was in Banu Salimah, and asked him about the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Madinah nine years without performing Hajj. Then it was announced among the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform Hajj this year. Many people descended upon Madinah, all seeking to follow the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and do as he did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out with five days remaining of Dhu al-Qadah, and we set out until we reached Dhu al-Hulayfah. Asma gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, so she sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What should I do? He said: Take a bath, wrap yourself with a cloth, then enter ihram. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out until, when his camel stood level with him on al-Bayda, he entered ihram with tawhid: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, You have no partner, here I am; praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; You have no partner. The people also recited talbiyah, the people adding words like possessor of lofty ranks and such speech, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard but said nothing to them. I looked as far as my sight reached before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): riders and walkers, the same behind him, the same on his right, the same on his left. Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us; the Quran was being revealed and he knew its interpretation, and whatever he did of it, we did. He said: We set out intending only Hajj, until when we reached the Kabah, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touched the Black Stone, then ran three circuits and walked four, until when he finished he went to the Station of Ibrahim and prayed two rakahs behind it, reciting: And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. He said: He recited in them al-Tawhid and Say: O disbelievers. Then he touched the Stone, then went out to al-Safa, then said: We begin with what Allah began with, and recited: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. He climbed al-Safa until, when he looked at the House, he magnified Allah, then said: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is dominion and His is praise, and He is over all things capable; there is no god but Allah alone; He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone. Then he supplicated and returned to these words, then descended until, when his feet poured into the valley, he ran, until when he ascended he walked, until when he reached al-Marwah he climbed it, until when he looked at the House he said upon it as he said upon al-Safa. When he was on the seventh at al-Marwah, he said: O people, had I known beforehand what I know now, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal and would have made it umrah; whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram and make it umrah. All the people exited ihram. Suraqah ibn Jushum said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year of ours or forever? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced his fingers, saying: Rather forever, three times; umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. Ali arrived from Yemen, bringing sacrificial animals with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had brought sacrificial animals with him from Madinah. Then Fatimah had exited ihram, wearing dyed clothes and kohl, saying: My father commanded me. Ali disapproved of that in her. He said: Jafar said: This phrase Jabir ibn Abdullah did not mention. Ali said in Kufah: I went forth disputing, seeking confirmation from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what Fatimah mentioned. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah has exited ihram, wearing dyed clothes and kohl, saying: My father commanded me with it. He said: She spoke the truth, she spoke the truth, she spoke the truth; I commanded her with it. Then he returned to the hadith of Jabir, saying to Ali: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger enters ihram with, and I have the sacrificial animal with me. He said: Then do not exit ihram. He said: The total of the sacrificial animals the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought and Ali brought was one hundred. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered sixty-three with his hand and gave to Ali, who slaughtered the rest, associating him in his sacrifice. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a piece from every camel, placed in a pot; they ate of its meat and drank of its broth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have sacrificed here, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice. He stood then said: I have stood here, and all of Arafah is a standing place. He stood at al-Muzdalifah and said: I have stood here, and all of al-Muzdalifah is a standing place."
"2129","Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ammar informed him, saying: I asked Jabir ibn Abdullah: Is the hyena eaten? He said: Yes. I said: Is it game? He said: Yes. I said: Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"2130","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: What I fear most for my nation after me is the deed of the people of Lut."
"2131","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out to Makkah in the year of the Conquest in Ramadan, fasting until he reached Kura al-Ghamim. He fasted Ramadan, and the people fasted with him. It was said to him: Fasting has been hard on the people, and they only look to what you do. He called for a cup of water after Asr and drank while the people watched. Some fasted and some broke fast. It reached him that some people fasted, and he said: Those are the disobedient."
"2132","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shintir, from Ata, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover vessels, tie water-skins, close doors, keep your children in at evening, for the jinn spread out and snatch; extinguish lamps at bedtime, for the mischievous mouse may drag the wick and burn the household."
"2133","Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which prayer is best? He said: Long standing."
"2134","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Sulayman, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waived liability for crop calamities."
"2135","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who raises his voice in lamentation, shaves his head, or tears his garment."
"2136","And from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, in a repeated narration: You today are upon a religion, and I will outnumber other nations through you, so do not turn back on your heels after me."
"2137","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Grazing livestock causing damage is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"2138","And from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will not guide you when they have gone astray; you will either affirm falsehood or deny truth. By Allah, were Musa alive among you, nothing would be lawful for him but to follow me."
"2139","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir: If you are given this, take it, and if you are not given it, beware - then he mentioned the two sons of Suriya, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them and said to them: By the One Who revealed the Torah to Musa, Who parted the sea, Who sent down to you manna and quails, do you know better? They said: Our people have granted us that. He said: One of them said: He adjures us with such. He said: You find a glance to be adultery, embracing to be adultery, kissing to be adultery; when four witness that they saw him entering and returning as the kohl stick enters the kohl container, then stoning."
"2140","Ishaq narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to us, a man of my people narrated to us, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given a gift and finds means, let him repay it; if he does not find means, let him praise the giver. Whoever praises him has thanked him; whoever conceals it has been ungrateful. Whoever adorns himself with what he was not given is like one wearing two garments of falsehood. He said with his finger like this: the index and middle."
"2141","Ishaq and al-Qawariri narrated to us, both saying: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdullah, freedman of Ghufrah, narrated to us, saying: I heard Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Safwan mentioning, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: O people, Allah has companies of angels who alight and stand over gatherings of remembrance on earth; graze in the meadows of Paradise. They said: What are the meadows of Paradise, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Gatherings of remembrance; go and return in the remembrance of Allah, and remember Him by yourselves. Whoever wishes to know his station with Allah, then Allah places the servant where he places Him in himself."
"2142","Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah, one who heard Jabir informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it."
"2143","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came visiting me on foot, neither riding a mule nor a horse."
"2144","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Salim ibn Hayyan, from Said ibn Mina: Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mukhabarah: leasing land for half."
"2145","And Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has surplus water or land, let him cultivate it or have his brother cultivate it; do not sell it. Sulaym said: I said: O Said, what does he mean by selling? Leasing? He said: Yes."
"2146","And he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens. I said to Jabir: What is ripening? He said: It turns red and yellow, and becomes edible."
"2147","Jabir narrated to us: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the Negus, pronouncing four takbirs."
"2148","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Karib, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"2149","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest wearing a black turban."
"2150","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafah with tranquillity, commanded tranquillity, hastened in the valley of Muhassir, and said: Take your rites, for I do not know whether you will meet me after this year or this day of yours; and he stoned with pebbles like those used for flinging."
"2151","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a donkey whose nostrils were smoking, branded on its face. He said: Did I not curse whoever did this? Let none brand on the face, nor strike on the face."
"2152","And from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Banu al-Najjar and heard a sound, then came out frightened, saying: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."
"2153","And from Jabir who said: On the day of al-Hudaybiyah we sacrificed seventy camels, each camel on behalf of seven; and he said: Let a group share in the sacrificial animal."
"2154","And from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim declared the House of Allah sacred and secure, and I have declared Madinah sacred; what is between its two lava plains is forbidden: its game is not hunted, its thorn trees are not cut."
"2155","And from Jabir and Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"2156","And from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The throne of Iblis is upon the sea; he sends out companies, and the greatest of them in his sight is the greatest of them in temptation."
"2157","And from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Iblis has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but he seeks to stir discord among you."
"2158","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and permitted horse meat."
"2159","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil who said: I heard Jabir say: Zuhr is as its name, Asr while the sun is bright and white, Maghrib as its name; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with us while we could see where arrows landed; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hasten Isha, and Fajr as its name."
"2160","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, that Banu Salimah mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the distance of their dwellings. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Salimah, keep your dwellings, for your footsteps are recorded."
"2161","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized a man on his inner elbow twice."
"2162","Shayban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ammar narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the hyena. He said: It is game; a ram is due for it if a pilgrim in ihram kills it."
"2163","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to an Ansari woman; she spread a mat for him near images and sprinkled around it, slaughtered a sheep and prepared food for him. He ate and we ate with him, then he performed ablution for Zuhr prayer and prayed. The woman said: O Messenger of Allah, some of our sheep meat remains; would you like supper? He said: Yes. He ate and we ate, then he prayed Asr without ablution."
"2164","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Jabir who said: A Jew held a debt of dates against my father; my father left two gardens, and the Jews dates encompassed both gardens. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Would you take part this year and defer part to next year? The Jew refused. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, when the harvest comes, inform me. I informed him; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with Abu Bakr and Umar. Dates were measured for him from the lower part of the palms, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for blessing. We paid him his due - Ammar said: I think from the smaller of the two gardens. He said: Then we brought them fresh dates; they ate and drank. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is of the bounty you will be questioned about."
"2165","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the radiant, white-limbed ones."
"2166","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: On the day of Taif, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a private conversation with Ali, prolonging it. Some of his companions said: He prolonged his private talk with his cousin. That reached him, and he said: It was not I who conversed with him privately; rather Allah did."
"2167","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day on the pulpit and said: O people, I did not stand among you with news that came to me from heaven; rather news reached me and I rejoiced at it, and I wished you to rejoice at the joy of your Prophet. While travellers were sailing in the sea, their food ran out; an island appeared to them, and they went out seeking bread. The Jassasah met them. I said to Abu Salamah: What is the Jassasah? He said: A woman dragging the hair of her skin and head. She said: In this palace is news of what you seek. They came to it and found a man bound. He said: Inform me, or ask me and I will inform you. The people fell silent. He said: Inform me about the palms of Baysan: do they bear fruit? They said: Yes. He said: Inform me about the lake of Zughar: is there water in it? They said: Yes. They said: He is the Messiah; the earth will be folded for him in forty days, except what is of Taybah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And Taybah is Madinah; there is no gate of its gates but an angel with unsheathed sword prevents him, and the same at Makkah. Then he said: In the sea of Persia it is, in the sea of Rome it is, three times. Then he struck his right palm upon his left three times. Ibn Abi Salamah said to me: In this hadith is something I did not memorize. We said: What is it? He said: Jabir testified that he is Ibn Said. I said: No, for Ibn Said has died. He said: Even if he died. I said: He has embraced Islam. He said: Even if he embraced Islam. I said: He entered Madinah. He said: Even if he entered Madinah."
"2168","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih and Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finishes his food, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."
"2169","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir, that a man freed a slave of his after his death. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy him from me? He said: Nuaym ibn Abdullah bought him; he took his price and handed it to him."
"2170","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Habib, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, with the same as the hadith of Husayn from Ata, adding in it: He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is poor, let him begin with himself."
"2171","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the perfection of prayer is straightening the row."
"2172","Abu Ali Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No townsman sells for a Bedouin; leave people, Allah provides for some of them through others."
"2173","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it becomes wholesome."
"2174","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is a partner in a property or palm trees has no right to sell it until he informs his partner; if he is pleased, he takes it, and if he dislikes, he leaves it."
"2175","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Harawi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out to reconcile between Banu Amr ibn Awf of the Ansar. He said: Prayer time came; Bilal said to Abu Bakr: Shall I call the adhan and you lead the people? He said: Yes. Bilal gave the iqamah; Abu Bakr stepped forward and led the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and they began clapping with their hands for Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr hardly ever turned in prayer; when they clapped, he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and stepped back. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him with his hand to pray, but he refused. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed. When he finished his prayer, he said to Abu Bakr: What prevented you from praying? He said: It is not for the son of Abu Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He turned to the people and said: What is this clapping? Clapping in prayer is only for women; when one of you has a need, let him say subhan Allah."
"2176","Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to me, that Jabir narrated to them, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Umm as-Sa'ib, or Umm al-Musayyib, while she was shivering with fever, and he said to her: What is the matter with you, O Umm as-Sa'ib, you are shivering? She said: Fever, may Allah put no blessing in it. He said: Do not curse it, for it removes the sins of the children of Adam just as the bellows remove the dross of iron."
"2177","Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: A man came to Madinah as an emigrant, he said: then he suffered a severe fever, and he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, release me from emigration. He said: No, by Allah, I will not release you; Islam is not to be released from. Al-Hajjaj said: and he mentioned that more than once, each time he refused him, then he left without his permission, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of him, and he said: It is Taybah; it expels the dross of men just as the bellows expel the dross of iron."
"2178","Ibrahim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: At-Tufayl ibn Amr ad-Dawsi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makkah, and said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Come to a strong fortress, with numbers and equipment. Abu az-Zubayr said: Daws is a fortress on a mountain top, reached only as through a sandal strap pass. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are those behind you with you? He said: I do not know. He said: So he turned away from him, because of what Allah had stored for the Ansar. He said: Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, At-Tufayl ibn Amr came emigrating to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him a man of his clan, and that man suffered a severe fever and went out, and took a blade and cut his insides with it, and bled profusely until he died, and he was buried, then he came in a dream at night to At-Tufayl ibn Amr in a fine appearance, with his hand covered, and At-Tufayl said to him: Is it you, so-and-so? He said: Yes. He said: How were you treated? He said: My Lord treated me well; He forgave me because of my emigration to His Prophet. He said: What happened to your hands? He said: My Lord said: We will never repair for you what you ruined of yourself. So At-Tufayl related his dream to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he raised his hand and said: O Allah, forgive him for his hands too; O Allah, forgive him for his hands too; O Allah, forgive him for his hands too."
"2179","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Umayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prostrate on the upper part of his forehead along with the hairline."
"2180","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand by a wooden post, leaning on it, delivering the sermon every Friday, until a man from Rome came to him and said: If you wish, I will make something for you such that when you sit on it, it is as if you are standing? He said: Yes. He said: So he made the minbar for him, and when he sat on it, the wooden post moaned like a she-camel moans for its calf, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down and placed his hand on it. Then the next day, I saw it had been moved, and we said: What is this? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with Abu Bakr and Umar and they moved it."
"2181","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay', from Abu Salamah, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us one day on the minbar and said: While some people were traveling in the sea, the Jassasah met them, and I said: What is the Jassasah? He said: A woman dragging the hair of her skin and head. She said: In this palace is the news of what you seek. So they came to it, and there they were with a man in chains. He said: Inform me, or ask me and I will inform you. The people fell silent. He said: Inform me about the palm trees of Baysan, and the spring of Zughar and Amman, has it borne fruit? They said: Yes. He said: Then inform me about the muddy hollow of Zughar, is there water in it? They said: Yes, it is full, its side overflowing. He said: Then he said: And he is the Masih; the earth will be folded for him and he will traverse it in forty, except what is of Taybah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is Madinah; there is no gate among its gates except upon it an angel with unsheathed sword preventing him from it, and the same for Makkah. Then he said: In the sea of Persia, what is it; in the sea of Rome, what is it, three times. He said: Ibn Abi Salamah said: There is something in this hadith that I did not memorize. He said: Then Jabir testified that he is Ibn Sayyad. He said: So I said: But Ibn Sayyad has died. He said: Even if he has died. He said: So I said: But he had accepted Islam. He said: Even if he had accepted Islam. He said: But he had entered Madinah. He said: Even if he had entered Madinah."
"2182","Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Hilali narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: We never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disclose to us anything of supplication over funerals, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar."
"2183","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Hisham ad-Dastawa'i narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I fell ill, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and blew on my face, and I recovered."
"2184","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail informed me, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that any of us lie down placing one of his legs upon the other."
"2185","Uqbah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will surely come upon people a time when an army from their armies goes out, and it will be said: Is there among you anyone who accompanied Muhammad, so you seek victory through him and are granted victory? Then it will be said: Is there among you one who accompanied Muhammad? It will be said: No; then who accompanied his Companions? It will be said: No. Then it will be said: Who saw one who accompanied his Companions? If they heard of him from beyond the sea, they would come to him."
"2186","Uqbah narrated to us, Mas'adah ibn al-Yasa' narrated to us, from Shibl ibn Abbad, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which of the people is most knowledgeable? He said: One who gathers the knowledge of people to his own knowledge, and every possessor of knowledge is still hungry for more."
"2187","Al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People will increase and my Companions will decrease, so do not revile them; may Allah curse whoever reviles them."
"2188","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir, he said: I was in the second or third row when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the Negus."
"2189","Masruq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Sulayk came to the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and he ordered him to pray two brief rak'ahs."
"2190","Masruq narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ayyub al-Afriqi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets were shown to me, and I most resemble Ibrahim."
"2191","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ja'far, from his father, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr at Arafat with one adhan and two iqamahs, and Maghrib and Isha with one adhan and two iqamahs."
"2192","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: He permitted them to cut palm trees, then was strict with them about it, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there sin upon us for what we cut, or upon us for what we left? So Allah sent down: Whatever you cut of the soft palm trees, or left standing upon their roots, it was by permission of Allah."
"2193","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Malih, Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Allah sent down the scriptures of Ibrahim on the first night of Ramadan, and the Torah was sent down upon Musa on six nights past of Ramadan, and the Psalms were sent down upon Dawud on eleven nights past of Ramadan, and the Qur'an was sent down upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on twenty-four nights past of Ramadan."
"2194","Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between a man, or he said, between a servant and disbelief is abandoning prayer."
"2195","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, from Jabir, he said: My maternal aunt was divorced, and she wanted to harvest her palm trees, but a man forbade her from going out to it, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Yes, go and harvest it, for perhaps you will give charity and do good."
"2196","Sufyan narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata informed me, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, and he mentioned withdrawal, and he said: We used to practice it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2197","Sufyan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse the night and the day, nor the sun and the moon, nor the winds, for they are sent as mercy for some people and punishment for others."
"2198","Sufyan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ath-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever revives a dead land, for him is reward in it, and whatever wild creatures eat is charity for him."
"2199","Sufyan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge with Allah from knowledge that does not benefit."
"2200","Sufyan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Usamah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people reciting the Qur'an in the mosque, and said: Recite the Qur'an before there comes a people who establish it like the straightening of an arrow shaft, seeking immediate gain with it and not seeking the Hereafter with it."
"2201","Sufyan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Ubayd al-Azdi, al-Fadl ar-Raqashi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood delivering the sermon on Friday and said: Perhaps a man whose Friday comes while he is a mile from Madinah, yet he does not attend Friday. He said: Then he said the second time: Perhaps a man whose Friday comes while he is two miles from Madinah, yet he does not attend it. And he said the third time: Perhaps he is three miles from Madinah, yet he does not attend Friday, and Allah seals his heart."
"2202","Sufyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah being asked about riding sacrificial camels, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ride it in a proper manner when you are forced to it, until you find another mount."
"2203","Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay', from Abu Salamah, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood one day on the minbar and said: While some people were traveling in the sea, their food ran out, and an island was raised before them, so they went out seeking bread, and the Jassasah met them. I said to Abu Salamah: What is the Jassasah? He said: A woman dragging the hair of her head. She said to them: In this palace is the news of what you seek. So they came to it, and there they were with a man in chains. He said: Inform me, or ask me and I will inform you. The people fell silent. He said: Inform me about the palm trees of Baysan and Ariha, or Ariha', has it borne fruit? They said: Yes. He said: Then inform me about the muddy hollow of Zughar, is there water in it? They said: Yes. They said: He is the Masih; the earth will be folded for him and he will traverse it in forty days, except what is of Taybah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Taybah is Madinah; there is no gate among its gates except an angel with unsheathed sword preventing him from it, and the same for Makkah. Then he said: In the sea of Persia, what is it; in the sea of Rome, what is it. Abu Salamah said to me: There is something in this hadith that I did not memorize. He said: Jabir ibn Abdullah testified that he is Ibn Sayyad. I said: But he has died. He said: Even if he has died. I said: But he accepted Islam. He said: Even if he accepted Islam. I said: But he had entered Madinah. He said: Even if he had entered Madinah."
"2204","Al-Husayn ibn Yazid at-Tahhan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu Talib, from Muharib, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent condiment is vinegar, and it suffices a man as evil that he disdains what is brought near to him."
"2205","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim al-Mafluj, reliable, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trotted from one stone to the other."
"2206","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: We were on a journey, and a man fasted and fainted, and his companions stood over him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed and they said: He fasted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness."
"2207","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ride it in a proper manner when you are forced to it, until you find another mount, meaning thereby the sacrificial camel."
"2208","Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Abu Bakr an-Nahshali narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Abi al-Haytham narrated to us, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the two jugular veins and between the shoulders, and gave the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given him."
"2209","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting Friday alone."
"2210","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd ar-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr al-Makki, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Abdullah about wheat for dates with excess, hand to hand, and he said: We used to, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), buy one sa' of wheat for six sa's of dates, hand to hand; but if it is one kind, there is no good in it except like for like."
"2211","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey in Ramadan, and he and his Companions came upon a pond, and he said to the people: Drink. They said: We drink while you do not drink? He said: I am the lightest of you; I am riding. Then he dismounted and drank, and they drank."
"2212","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, the people of the cross who collect fats came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we collect these fats from carrion and other than it, and they are only for seasoning and ships. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and consumed their prices. Then he forbade them from that."
"2213","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever supports three daughters, sufficing them, having mercy on them and being gentle with them, is in Paradise. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. Until we said: If a person had said: And one, he would have said: And one."
"2214","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id al-Qassam narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand one day until he came to one of the rooms of his wives, and entered, then gave me permission and I entered, and he said: Is there any lunch, or is there any dinner? They said: Yes. Then three loaves were brought, and he said: Is there any condiment? They said: No, except some vinegar. He said: Bring it, for what an excellent condiment is vinegar. Jabir said: I have loved it ever since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying this about it. Abu Sufyan said: And I have loved it ever since I heard Jabir saying what he says."
"2215","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid informed us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Ata, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man speaks to people and then turns away, it is a trust."
"2216","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who plants a planting except it is charity for him: whatever is eaten of it, whatever is stolen of it, whatever birds eat of it, and whatever wild beasts eat of it."
"2217","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is valid for the one to whom it is granted, and Ruqba is valid for the one to whom it is granted."
"2218","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, he said: Talhah ibn Nafi' narrated to me, from Jabir, he said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they spoke of him and praised him, and he said: Who will kill him? Abu Bakr said: I will. So he went and found him having drawn a line around himself, standing praying in it. When he saw him in that state, he returned and did not kill him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will kill him? Umar said: I will. So he went and saw him praying, standing in a line praying, and returned and did not kill him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is for him, or who will kill him? Ali said: I will. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You, but I do not think you will reach him. So he went and found him gone."
"2219","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, that Shurahbil ibn Sa'd informed him, from Jabir, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the time of Hudaybiyah, and we camped at as-Suqya, and Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: Who will draw water for us into our waterskins? Jabir said: So I said: I will. I went out with some youths with me until we came to the water at al-Uthayah, and between them was nearly twenty-three miles. He said: We came to the water at al-Uthayah and drew water into our trough and into our waterskins, until when it was after nightfall, I saw a man whose camel was disputing with him at the trough, and he said: Bring to water. And there he was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he watered and took the bridle of his mount, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed Isha, with Jabir, as he mentioned, beside him, then prayed after Isha thirteen rak'ahs."
"2220","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman at-Taymi informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you of a living soul upon whom a hundred years come while it is alive."
"2221","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab informed us, Abu Sufyan Talhah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: I was sitting in my house when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me and gestured to me, so I stood to him, and he took my hand and we went until he came to one of the rooms of his wives, and entered, then gave me permission and I entered, with the curtain upon her, and he said: Is there any lunch? They said: Yes. Then three loaves were brought and he placed them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a loaf and placed it before himself, and took another loaf and placed it before me, then took the third and broke it in two, placing half before himself and half before me, then said: Is there any condiment? They said: No, except some vinegar. He said: Bring it, for what an excellent condiment it is."
"2222","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from al-Hasan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are in fertile land, give the mounts their share of their feet, and do not pass beyond the stopping places. And when you are in drought, hasten, and upon you is night travel, for the earth is folded at night. When the ghouls appear to you, hasten with the adhan. Do not pray on the main roads, nor camp upon them, for they are the abode of snakes and predators, and do not relieve yourselves upon them, for they are places of curses."
"2223","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Jabir, he said: A man came with an egg of gold to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which he had found in one of the expeditions, and said: Take it, O Messenger of Allah, as charity; by Allah, I own nothing else this morning. He turned away from him, then he came to him from his left and said the like, then he came to him from before him and said the like, and he said: Bring it, angrily. He took it and threw it at him with a throw that, had it hit him, would have wounded or gored him, then said: One of you comes with all his wealth and gives it in charity, then sits begging from people. Indeed there is no charity except from surplus wealth."
"2224","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the barking of dogs and the braying of donkeys, seek refuge with Allah from Satan, for they see what you do not see. Lessen going out when the foot traffic quiets, for Allah spreads among His creation at His night what He wills. Close the doors, for Satan does not open a closed door. Tie the waterskins, cover the vessels, and extinguish the lamps."
"2225","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Ata, and from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham al-Juhfah, for the people of Yemen Yalamlam, for the people of Ta'if Qarn, and for the people of Iraq Dhat Irq."
"2226","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In animals, two for one is no harm, but it is not valid on credit."
"2227","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Ata, from Jabir, that a man vowed to pray in Bayt al-Maqdis, and he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said to him: Pray here, meaning the Sacred Mosque. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I only vowed to pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Pray here. He said: And I think he said the third time: Pray where you said."
"2228","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Amr al-Awza'i narrated to me, he said: I heard Yahya saying: I asked Abu Salamah, which Qur'an was sent down first? He said: O you wrapped up. I said: Or Read. Jabir said: I narrate to you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us. He said: I stayed in seclusion at Hira for a month, and when I completed my seclusion, I came down and went into the valley, and I was called, and I looked before me and behind me, and on my right and on my left, and saw no one. Then I was called and looked and saw no one. Then I was called and looked and saw no one. Then I raised my head, and there he was upon the throne in the air, meaning Jibril. A severe trembling seized me, and I came to Khadijah and said: Wrap me up. So they wrapped me and poured water over me, and Allah sent down: O you wrapped up, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your garments purify."
"2229","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, Hisham ad-Dastawa'i narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade onions and leeks. He said: Need overcame us, so we ate of them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this foul tree, let him not approach our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what humans, or he said, the children of Adam, are harmed by."
"2230","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mukhawwal, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed, he poured over his head three times. A man from Banu Hashim said: My hair is abundant. He said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more abundant than your hair, and better."
"2231","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote upon every clan its blood-money, then wrote that it is not lawful for the freedman of a Muslim man to take another as master without his permission."
"2232","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir saying: We used to sell our slave concubines who were mothers of children, with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alive among us, and he saw no harm in that."
"2233","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya and Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us, both said: Abu az-Zubayr informed us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me for a need, and I returned while he was upon his mount, and I greeted him but he did not return anything to me. And Zakariyya added: Then I greeted him and he did not return anything to me. Then their narrations agreed thereafter: I saw him bowing and prostrating, so I moved away from him. Then he said: What did you do about your need? I said: I did such and such. He said: Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was praying. And Zakariyya added: When he finished his prayer, he called me and returned the greeting to me, and said: I was praying."
"2234","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that any animal be killed by confinement."
"2235","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabil narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu az-Zubayr narrating from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Qur'an: In the name of Allah, greetings, prayers and good things belong to Allah; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I ask Allah for Paradise, and I seek refuge with Allah from the Fire."
"2236","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Hajjaj as-Sawwaf narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah the Magnificent, and with His praise, a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."
"2237","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you buries his brother, let him make his shroud good."
"2238","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade branding on the face and striking on the face."
"2239","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir, that a man freed a slave of his as a mudabbar after his death, and the man became needy, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy him from me? So Nu'aym ibn Abdullah bought him, and he took its price and gave it to him."
"2240","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): For every prophet there is a supplication he has made for his nation, and I have hidden my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"2241","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata said, I heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine fresh ripe dates with unripe dates, nor raisins with dried dates."
"2242","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took part in twenty-one expeditions."
"2243","Abu az-Zubayr said, Jabir said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Aqabah."
"2244","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir saying: I fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in nineteen expeditions. Jabir said: I did not witness Badr nor Uhud; my father prevented me. He said: When Abdullah was killed on the day of Uhud, I never stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in any expedition."
"2245","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cleaning oneself with a bone or with dung."
"2246","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah narrating: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to carry stones with them for the Ka'bah while his lower garment was upon him, and al-Abbas, his uncle, said to him: O son of my brother, if you loosened your lower garment and placed it upon your shoulder beneath the stones? He said: So he loosened it and placed it upon his shoulder. He said: Then he fell unconscious. He said: He was never seen naked after that day."
"2247","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr informed us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah claiming: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pictures in the house, and forbade a man to make that."
"2248","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim man plants a planting or sows a crop, and a beast, bird or anything eats of it, except there is reward for him in it."
"2249","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you wipe with a cloth until he licks his hand, for he does not know in which of his food blessing is placed for him. Satan lies in wait for people at everything, even at their food. Let him not lift the bowl until he licks it, for the last of the food contains blessing."
"2250","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you tastes food and his morsel falls from his hand, let him remove what is doubtful, then eat it, and not leave it for Satan, for a man does not know in which of his food blessing is placed for him."
"2251","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break fast; if it is obscured for you, count thirty days."
"2252","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept away from his wives for a month, then came out on the morning of the twenty-ninth. Some of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, we have reached the morning of the twenty-ninth? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is twenty-nine. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clapped with his hands three times, twice with all the fingers, and the third with nine of them."
"2253","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to forbid being named Barakah, Aflah, Yasar, Nafi', and the like, then I saw him thereafter fall silent about it and say nothing. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away without forbidding that. Then Umar wanted to forbid that, then left it."
"2254","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ismail informed me, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir, he said: When Safiyyah bint Huyayy came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his tent, people were present, and I was present with them that I might have a share in it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: Stand away from your mother. When it was evening, we were present, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out in his cloak with about a mudd and a half of Ajwa dates. He said: Eat from the wedding feast of your mother."
"2255","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an expedition he fought, in Ramadan, and a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted and became severely weak, and thirst almost killed him, and his she-camel kept entering the thorny trees. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of him and said: Bring him to me. He was brought to him, and he said: Are you not in the path of Allah, and with the Messenger of Allah? Break your fast. So he broke fast."
"2256","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: Abu Bakr as-Siddiq came seeking permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found people sitting at his door, none of them given permission. He said: Permission was given to Abu Bakr and he entered. Then Umar came and sought permission and was given permission, and found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting with his wives around him, gloomy and silent. He said: I shall surely say something to make the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laugh. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if you had seen the daughter of Kharijah asking me for maintenance, I stood to her and struck her neck. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: They are around me as you see, asking me for maintenance. Then Abu Bakr stood to A'ishah striking her neck, and Umar stood to Hafsah striking her neck, each saying: You ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for what he does not have? They said: By Allah, we shall never ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for anything he does not have. Then he kept away from them for a month or twenty-nine days. Then this verse came down upon him: O Prophet, say to your wives, until it reached: For the doers of good among you a great reward. He said: He began with A'ishah and said: O A'ishah, I want to present a matter to you; I do not want you to hasten in anything about it until you consult your parents. She said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He recited the verse to her. She said: About you, O Messenger of Allah, should I consult my parents? Rather I choose Allah and His Messenger and the Hereafter. And I ask you not to inform any of your wives of what I said. He said: No woman among them will ask me except I will inform her; Allah did not send me as one who causes hardship, but sent me as a teacher and facilitator."
"2257","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd as-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wear the salla' wrap in a single garment, let none of you eat with his left hand, let none walk in a single sandal, and let none sit with knees drawn up in a single garment."
"2258","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd as-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: We practiced withdrawal in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not forbid us from it."
"2259","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd as-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Makki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave marries without the permission of his master, he is a fornicator."
"2260","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd as-Samad narrated to us, Kathir narrated to us, Ata narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, and I went and returned having completed it. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, but he did not return it to me, and there entered my heart what Allah knows best. He said: I said: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is displeased with me because I was slow. Then I greeted him and he did not return it to me, and there entered my heart worse than the first. Then I greeted him and he returned it to me, and said: Nothing prevented me from returning it to you except that I was praying, and he was upon his mount facing other than the qiblah."
"2261","Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, that Jabir ibn Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover the vessel, tie the waterskin, and extinguish the lamp, for Satan does not untie a waterskin, nor open a door, nor uncover a vessel. If one of you finds nothing but to place a stick over his vessel and mention Allah, let him do so, for the mouse sets fire to the house upon its people."
"2262","Kamil narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr said: Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not eat with the left hand, for Satan eats with the left hand."
"2263","Kamil narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade wrapping in a single garment, and sitting with knees drawn up in a single garment, and that a man raise one of his legs over the other while lying on his back."
"2264","Kamil narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the prophets were shown to me: Musa was a lean man of men, as if from the men of Shanu'ah. I saw Isa, and the one I saw most resembling him was Urwah ibn Mas'ud. I saw Ibrahim, and the one I saw most resembling him was your companion, meaning himself. I saw Jibril, and the one I saw most resembling him was Dihyah."
"2265","Kamil narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan cannot take my form. And he said: When one of you dreams, let him not inform people of Satan toying with him in sleep."
"2266","Kamil narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When one of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times, seek refuge with Allah from Satan three times, and turn from the side he was upon."
"2267","Kamil narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept away from his wives for a month, then came out on the night of the twenty-ninth. We said: Only twenty-nine have passed. He said: The month is like this. And he clapped three times, and withheld one finger at the last."
"2268","Kamil narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that he informed him, that Hatib ibn Abi Balta'ah wrote to the people of Makkah mentioning that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to raid them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was guided to the woman with whom the letter was, and he sent to her, and her letter was taken from her head. He said: O Hatib, did you do it? He said: Yes. But I did not do it out of treachery to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor hypocrisy. I knew that Allah would make His Messenger victorious and complete His matter for him. But I was among them, and my mother was with them, so I wanted to gain favor with them. Umar said to him: Shall I not strike the neck of this one? He said: Would you kill a man of the people of Badr? What do you know, perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish?"
"2269","Kamil narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best toward which mounts are ridden are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."
"2270","Kamil narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that Umm Salamah sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for cupping, and he ordered Abu Taybah and he cupped her. Abu Ya'la said: I think he said: He was her brother through suckling."
"2271","Kamil narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Abu az-Zubayr, freedman of Hakim ibn Hizam, narrated to me, from Jabir: that when they were present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would send the sacrificial animals; whoever of us wished entered ihram, and whoever of us wished refrained."
"2272","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies upon something, Allah will resurrect him upon it."
"2273","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise eat and drink therein, yet do not defecate, nor urinate, nor blow their noses; rather it is perspiration of musk."
"2274","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, and my father, both said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever believer I insult or curse, make it purification and reward for him."
"2275","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in good and evil."
"2276","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which of the Muslims is best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe."
"2277","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw in a dream as if my head was cut off. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: When Satan plays with one of you in his sleep, let him not narrate it to people."
"2278","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the dog and the cat. Al-A'mash said: I think Abu Sufyan mentioned it."
"2279","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him pray two rak'ahs, shortening them."
"2280","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I live, Allah willing, I will command, or forbid my nation that they not name Aflah, nor Nafi', nor Barakah. Al-A'mash said: I do not know whether he mentioned Nafi' or not, because when a man comes and says: Is there Barakah? They say: No."
"2281","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What are the two that necessitate? He said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah enters the Fire."
"2282","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Ya'la narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you fears he will not pray witr at the end of the night, let him pray witr at its beginning; for recitation at the end of the night is attended, and it is better."
"2283","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ya'la and Muhammad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon A'ishah while a boy was with her whose nostrils dripped blood. She said: He has udhrah. He said: Do not kill your children; rather, whatever woman has a boy with udhrah, or pain in his head, let her take Indian costus, then grind it with water, then administer it through his nose. Then he ordered A'ishah and she did that, and he recovered."
"2284","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the night there is an hour no Muslim meets asking Allah for good except He gives it to him, and that is every night."
"2285","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ya'la narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was ordered to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"2286","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ya'la narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food blessing lies."
"2287","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ya'la narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him take it and not leave it for Satan."
"2288","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced, and not spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."
"2289","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you finishes prayer in the mosque, let him make for his house a portion of his prayer, for Allah will place in his house good from his prayer."
"2290","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b complained, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a physician to him, and he cauterized him on his basilic vein."
"2291","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut a vein of Ubayy ibn Ka'b and cauterized him on his basilic vein."
"2292","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of one man suffices two, the food of two men suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."
"2293","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying three days before his death, saying: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah."
"2294","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Madinah there are men; you travel no journey nor cross any valley except they were with you; excuse detained them."
"2295","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the prayers is the example of a flowing river at the door of one of you; he bathes from it every day five times."
"2296","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Awanah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan hears remembrance of Allah, he goes away until he is at the place of ar-Rawha'."
"2297","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Satan has despaired that the worshippers will worship him, but through stirring discord among them."
"2298","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: An Ansari man called an-Nu'man ibn Qawqal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me: if I pray the prescribed prayers, deem lawful and deem unlawful the unlawful, and add nothing to that, shall I enter Paradise? He said: Yes."
"2299","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man asked him: Which prayer is best? He said: Lengthy standing."
"2300","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse and his leg was bruised. We entered upon him while he was praying, and he gestured to us with his hand. Then we entered the next day while he was praying the prescribed prayer sitting, and he gestured to us with his hand to sit. Then he turned and said: When the imam is sitting, pray sitting; and when he prays standing, pray standing."
"2301","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man or woman, male or female, who sleeps at night except upon his head is a rope knotted. If he wakes and remembers Allah, a knot is loosened. If he stands, performs ablution and prays, all his knots are loosened, and he mornings energetic, having attained good. If he sleeps not remembering Allah, he mornings with his knots heavy upon him."
"2302","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ruqyahs. Then my maternal uncle came to him, and he used to treat scorpion stings with ruqyah, and said: You forbade ruqyahs, yet I treat scorpion stings with ruqyah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"2303","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Qutbah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perfume the dead with incense, do so an odd number of times."
"2304","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: We pledged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under the tree that we would not flee."
"2305","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhadir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You came asking me about such and such? We said: Yes. He said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah. He said: And you mentioned the Hour? We said: That had happened. He said: There is no living soul upon whom a hundred years come."
"2306","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of palms, he would wish for another like it; and nothing fills his belly except dust."
"2307","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: There was a slave girl of Abdullah ibn Ubayy called Musaykah, and he forced her. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of that to him, and Allah sent down: Do not force your slave girls into prostitution, if they desire chastity, to seek the goods of the life of this world."
"2308","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhadir narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believing man or woman, no Muslim man or woman falls ill except Allah removes his sins thereby."
"2309","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhadir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A detachment will be sent, and it will be said to them: Is there among you anyone who accompanied Muhammad? It will be said: Yes. He will be sought and found, a man, and victory will be sought through him and granted to them. Then a detachment will be sent, and it will be said: Is there among you one who saw the Companions of Muhammad? He will be sought and not found, until even if he were beyond the sea you would come to him. Then there will remain a people who recite the Qur'an, not knowing what it is."
"2310","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhadir narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his journey, and a wind blew nearly burying the rider. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wind was sent for the death of a hypocrite. When we arrived at Madinah, a great one of the great hypocrites had died that day."
"2311","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhadir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man perform ablution but water did not reach his heel, and said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"2312","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is among the people of Hijaz, and harshness and hardness are in Rabi'ah and Mudar."
"2313","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a battle, and a foul wind blew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are some hypocrites who mentioned people and backbit them."
"2314","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Ya'la narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Abu Sa'id, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying upon a mat and prostrating upon it. And I entered upon him while he was praying wrapped in a garment."
"2315","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that Umar saw a man perform ablution leaving the place of a nail upon his foot, and ordered him to repeat."
"2316","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that he was asked about a man who laughs in prayer, and he said: He repeats the prayer, but does not repeat ablution."
"2317","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Had I entered upon people praying, I would not have greeted them."
"2318","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I used to draw water for my companions on the day of Badr."
"2319","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: When he enters his grave, meaning the dead, the angel comes to him, and he rises startled as a sleeper rises. They question him and he answers them. They say: What is your religion? He says: Islam. Leave me that I may go out. They say to him: Be silent."
"2320","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, he said: I asked Jabir while he was residing in Makkah, staying among Banu Fihr. A man asked him: Did you call anyone of the people of the qiblah a polytheist? He said: Allah forbid. He was startled at that. He said: Did you call anyone among you a disbeliever? He said: No."
"2321","554 - (2318) - Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Qabisah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, raising it [to the Prophet], he said: He used to say: O Turner of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us, when we have believed in what you came with? He said: Hearts are between - and al-A'mash gestured with two fingers."
"2322","555 - (2319) - Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yala narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and it was said to him: Fever has pressed hard upon us. He said: If you wish that it be lifted from you, it will be lifted; and if you wish, it will be a purification for you? They said: Let it be a purification for us."
"2323","556 - (2320) - Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah said to me: Your cousin al-Hasan ibn Muhammad asked me about the bath for major impurity, so I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour water with his hand over his head three times. He said: My hair is thick. He said: I said: O son of my brother, the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was thicker than your hair and better."
"2324","557 - (2321) - Abu Said al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned garlic and onion, or one of them, and said: The angels are harmed by what the son of Adam is harmed by."
"2325","558 - (2322) - Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth mention, from Ata, from Jabir: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats garlic, onion and leek, let him not come near our mosque."
"2326","559 - (2323) - Abu Said al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If mature sheep are hard for you [to find], a young sheep suffices."
"2327","560 - (2324) - Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not slaughter except a mature animal, unless it is difficult for you, then slaughter a young sheep."
"2328","561 - (2325) - Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Misar, he heard it from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir, he said: He forbade [mixing] unripe dates with ripe dates, and raisins with dates."
"2329","562 - (2326) - Abu Said al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"2330","563 - (2327) - Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you hear the barking of dogs at night or the braying of donkeys, seek refuge with Allah, for they see what you do not see. And go out less when people have settled down, for Allah sends out at night of His creation what He wills. And close the doors and mention the name of Allah over them, for Satan does not open a door that has been closed with the name of Allah mentioned over it. And cover the jars, turn over the vessels, and tie the waterskins."
"2331","Beginning of the Musnad of Ibn Abbas. 1 - (2328) - Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili reported to us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas preaching on the pulpit of Basrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet except that he had a supplication he hastened in this world, and I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection. And I am the master of the children of Adam, without pride. And I am the first for whom the earth will split open, without pride. In my hand is the banner of praise, and Adam and those below him are under my banner, without pride. And the Day of Resurrection will be long upon the people and severe, until some of them say to others: Come with us to Adam, the father of mankind, so he may intercede for us with our Lord so He judges between us. So they go to Adam and say: O Adam, intercede for us with your Lord so He judges between us. So Adam says: I am not there for it; I was expelled from Paradise because of my sin, and today nothing concerns me except myself. But go to Nuh. So they say: O Nuh, intercede for us with your Lord so He judges between us. So he says: I am not there for you; I made a supplication that drowned the people of the earth, and today nothing concerns me except myself. But go to Ibrahim, the close friend of the Merciful. So they come to Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and say: O Ibrahim, intercede for us with your Lord so He judges between us. So he says: I am not there for you; I told three lies in Islam: his saying: Indeed I am sick, and his saying: Rather the greatest of them did it, and his saying to the king when he passed by him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, he intended by them nothing but honor for the religion of Allah. For today nothing concerns me except myself. But go to Musa, a servant whom Allah chose with His message and spoke to. So they come to Musa and say: O Musa, intercede for us with your Lord so He judges between us. So he says: I am not there for you; I killed a soul, and today nothing concerns me except myself. But go to Isa, the spirit of Allah and His word. So they come to Isa and say: O Isa, intercede for us with your Lord so He judges between us. So he says: I am not there for you; I was taken as a god besides Allah, and today nothing concerns me except myself. Have you considered: if there were goods in a sealed vessel, could what is in it be reached until the seal is broken? They say: No. So he says: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the seal of the prophets, and he has come, and Allah has forgiven him his past and future sins. So they come to me and say: O Muhammad, intercede for us with your Lord so He judges between us. So I say: I am for it, until Allah gives permission to whom He wills and is pleased with. So when Allah intends to judge between His creation, a caller will call: Where is Ahmad and his nation? Where is Ahmad and his nation? So they come, and we are the first and the last: the last to be raised, and the first to be judged. The nations will make way for us from our path, and we will proceed shining white from the traces of purification. So the nations will say: This nation was almost all prophets."
"2332","2 - (2329) - Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Rabah ibn Zayd reported to us, from Umar ibn Habib, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing Allah created was the Pen, and He commanded it and it wrote everything."
"2333","3 - (2330) - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was commanded with the tooth-stick so much that I thought a Quran or revelation would come down to me about it."
"2334","4 - (2331) - Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your brothers were struck at Uhud, Allah placed their souls in the bellies of green birds that visit the rivers of Paradise and eat from its fruits, and shelter in lamps of gold hung in the shade of the Throne. So when they found the goodness of their food, drink and rest, they said: Who will convey from us to our brothers that we are alive in Paradise being provided for, so they do not shrink back in battle nor lose interest in striving? He said: So Allah said: I will convey from you to them. So Allah, blessed and exalted, sent down: Do not think those killed in the way of Allah are dead; rather they are alive with their Lord - to the end of the verse."
"2335","5 - (2332) - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began speaking eloquent speech. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom."
"2336","6 - (2333) - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no contagion, no bad omen, no hama and no safar. So a man said to him: We take a mangy sheep and throw it among the sheep and they become mangy. He said: Then who infected the first?"
"2337","7 - (2334) - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A sheep belonging to Sawdah bint Zamah died, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died, meaning the sheep. He said: Why did you not take its skin? She said: Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He only said: Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me forbidden for one who eats it - the verse - there is no harm in tanning it and benefiting from it. She said: So she sent for it, skinned it, and took a waterskin from it until it wore out."
"2338","8 - (2335) - al-Mualla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umm Hufayd, my aunt, daughter of al-Harith, gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, dried yogurt and lizards. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for them and they were eaten at his table, while he left them as if finding them distasteful. Had they been unlawful, they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor would he have ordered eating them."
"2339","9 - (2336) - Jafar ibn Humayd al-Kufi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever existed in the pre-Islamic age, Islam only increased it in strength - or severity."
"2340","10 - (2337) - al-Mualla narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that a man was thrown by his camel and killed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he be washed with water and lote-leaves, not be touched with perfume, not be shrouded, and his head not be covered. And he said: He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with his hair matted."
"2341","11 - (2338) - al-Mualla narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of narrating from me except what you know, for whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire; and whoever lies about the Quran without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2342","12 - (2339) - Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only hastened around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah to show the people his strength."
"2343","13 - (2340) - Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never performed an umrah except in Dhu al-Qadah."
"2344","14 - (2341) - Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Khaybar, he handed over its land and palm trees on sharecropping for half."
"2345","15 - (2342) - Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdah and Humayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Aishah narrated to me: A thief's hand was not cut in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except for the value of a hajafah or a shield."
"2346","16 - (2343) - Uthman narrated to us, Husayn ibn Isa al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the best of you call the adhan, and let your reciters lead you in prayer."
"2347","17 - (2344) - Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Said ibn Yazid, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever is pleased to forbid what Allah and His Messenger forbade, let him forbid the nabidh of the earthen jar."
"2348","18 - (2345) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not go out to meet (caravans), do not leave milk unmilked (to deceive), and let none of you raise the price for another."
"2349","19 - (2346) - Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf and others narrated to us, they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah prescribed prayer upon the tongue of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): in residence four, in travel two, and in fear one."
"2350","20 - (2347) - Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Jad Abu Uthman al-Yashkuri narrated to us, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Ibn Abbas, reporting it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sees in his ruler something he dislikes, let him be patient, for whoever separates from the community by a span and dies, dies a death of ignorance."
"2351","21 - (2348) - Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks a drink until it takes away the mind Allah gave him has come to one of the doors of the major sins."
"2352","22 - (2349) - Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to us, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas; Hammad said: I do not know except that he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The bonds of Islam and the foundations of the religion are three, upon which Islam was founded; whoever abandons one of them is thereby a disbeliever whose blood is lawful: testifying that there is no god but Allah, the prescribed prayer, and fasting Ramadan. Then Ibn Abbas said: You find him with much wealth not paying zakat, so he remains thereby a disbeliever whose blood is lawful; and you find him with much wealth not performing hajj, so he remains thereby a disbeliever, but his blood is not lawful."
"2353","23 - (2350) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man from Banu Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who used to treat and remedy, and said to him: O Muhammad, you say things; shall I treat you? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him, then said to him: Would you like me to show you a sign? And near him were palm trees and trees. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a cluster from them, and it came toward him prostrating and rising, prostrating and raising its head, until it reached him and stood before him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to it: Return to your place, so it returned to its place. So he said: By Allah, I will never deny anything you say after this. Then he said: O Amir ibn Sasah, by Allah I will never deny him in anything he says after this ever. He said: And al-adhq is the palm tree."
"2354","24 - (2351) - Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man unable to perform hajj; shall I perform hajj on his behalf? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, perform hajj in place of your father."
"2355","25 - (2352) - Khalaf narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder, then wiped his hand with a cloth that was under him, then stood and prayed."
"2356","26 - (2353) - Khalaf narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to go out on a journey, he said: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from burdensome company in travel and gloom in the return. O Allah, gather the earth for us and make travel easy for us. And when he intended to return he said: Returning, worshipping, praising our Lord. And when he entered among his family he said: Repentance, repentance; to our Lord a return, leaving no sin upon us."
"2357","27 - (2354) - Khalaf narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People from my nation will recite the Quran, passing out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game."
"2358","28 - (2355) - Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast before Ramadan; fast upon seeing it and break upon seeing it; and if clouds come between you and it, complete thirty."
"2359","29 - (2356) - And with its chain from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not go out to meet the market, do not leave milk unmilked, and let none of you raise the price for another."
"2360","30 - (2357) - And from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a khumrah (small mat)."
"2361","31 - (2358) - Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to me, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When: Perish the hands of Abu Lahab was sent down, the wife of Abu Lahab came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr was with him. When Abu Bakr saw her he said: O Messenger of Allah, she is a foul-tongued woman and I fear she will harm you; if only you would stand. So he said: She will not see me. So she said: O Abu Bakr, your companion has lampooned me. He said: He does not speak poetry. She said: You are truthful in my view. And she left. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, she did not see you? He said: An angel kept screening me from her with his wing."
"2362","32 - (2359) - Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Shatha, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every division that was divided stands as it was divided, and every division that Islam reached stands as it was divided."
"2363","33 - (2360) - Ziyad ibn Ayyub Abu Hashim known as Dallawayh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram, on the two jugular veins and the upper back, and he gave the cupper his wage; had it been unlawful he would not have given him."
"2364","34 - (2361) - Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A righteous dream is a part - I think he said - of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"2365","35 - (2362) - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage."
"2366","36 - (2363) - Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Thaqafi, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A delegation of Banu Asad came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they spoke eloquently, and said: O Messenger of Allah, all of Mudar fought you and we did not fight you, and we are neither the fewest of them in number nor the weakest in strength, and we have joined your kinship. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr and Umar when he heard their speech: Do they speak like this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, their understanding is little, and Satan speaks upon their tongues."
"2367","37 - (2364) - Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep belonging to Sawdah bint Zamah died, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died, meaning the sheep. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not take its skin? She said: Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me forbidden - to - or the flesh of swine. Which of you eats it? That is: tan it and benefit from it. He said: So she sent for it, skinned it, tanned it, and took a waterskin from it until it wore out with her."
"2368","38 - (2365) - Yaqub ibn Mahan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says: When I take the two precious things of My servant and he is patient and expects reward, I am not pleased with a reward for him less than Paradise."
"2369","39 - (2366) - Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah's anger was severe upon one whom the Prophet of Allah killed in the way of Allah, and Allah's anger was severe upon people who bloodied the face of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2370","40 - (2367) - Said ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, he said: Ibn Abbas informed me that Ali, al-Fadl and Usamah entered the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Marhab informed me that they brought in Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, so it is as if I am looking at them in the grave, four. Al-Shabi said: And who attends to a man except his family."
"2371","41 - (2368) - Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal and Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and stayed nineteen [days] shortening the prayer. He said: So when we travel and stay nineteen we shorten the prayer, and if we exceed that we complete it."
"2372","42 - (2369) - And from Abu Awanah, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not recite to the jinn nor see them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out with a group of his companions heading to the market of Ukaz, while the devils had been barred from the news of heaven and flames sent against them. So the devils returned to their people, and they said: What is wrong with you? They said: We have been barred from the news of heaven and flames were sent upon us. He said: That is only because of something that happened, so strike the easts of the earth and its wests. So the group that took toward Tihamah passed - while he was at Nakhlah - heading to the market of Ukaz, while he was praying Fajr with his companions. When they heard the Quran they listened to it and said: This is what came between us and the news of heaven. So they returned to their people and said: O our people, we have heard an amazing Quran guiding to right guidance, so we believed in it. So Allah revealed to His Prophet: Say: It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened."
"2373","43 - (2370) - Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hayyan ibn Ubaydullah ibn Hayyan Abu Zuhayr al-Adawi narrated to us, Abu Mijlaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: And Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father: that the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was black and his flag was white."
"2374","44 - (2371) - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the fixed shares to those entitled to them; what remains is for the nearest male relative."
"2375","45 - (2372) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To the Book of Allah, to His Prophet, and to the leaders of the Muslims."
"2376","46 - (2373) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah - when he finished from Badr - go after the caravan, there is nothing before it. He said: So al-Abbas called to him: It is not right. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why? He said: Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you."
"2377","47 - (2374) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Utbah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Taif, he stopped at Jiranah, distributed the spoils there, then performed umrah from it, and that was with two nights remaining of Shawwal."
"2378","48 - (2375) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Masruq, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and stopped to rest at night, then slept and did not wake except by the sun. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, and he called the adhan, then he prayed two rakahs. Ibn Abbas said: The world and what is in it would not please me as much as it, meaning the concession."
"2379","49 - (2376) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hadirah al-Azdi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Sacrificial camels were few in the time of the Messenger of Allah, so he ordered the people to use cattle."
"2380","50 - (2377) - Hajjaj ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The People of the Book used to let their hair hang down and the idolaters used to part their heads. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to agree with the People of the Book in some matters about which he had not been commanded, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let his forelock hang down, then parted it afterwards."
"2381","51 - (2378) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at a man who approaches a man or a woman in the anus."
"2382","52 - (2379) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Makkah, Ali brought out the daughter of Hamzah. So Ali, Zayd and Jafar disputed over her. Ali said: The daughter of my brother, and I have most right to her. Jafar said: The daughter of my uncle, and her maternal aunt is with me. Zayd said: The daughter of my brother Hamzah, between whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Zayd, you are my freedman and theirs. And he said to Ali: You are my brother and my companion. And he said to Jafar: You resemble my creation and character, and she goes to her maternal aunt."
"2383","53 - (2380) - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from a vessel with a bent [spout]."
"2384","54 - (2381) - Abu Bakr narrated to us, al-Hudhayl ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Rawwad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The death of a stranger is martyrdom."
"2385","55 - (2382) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I and al-Fadl were on a she-donkey, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at Arafah. So we passed in front of part of the row, dismounted from it, left it grazing in the row, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said nothing to us."
"2386","56 - (2383) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Sad ibn Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a vow that was upon his mother who died before fulfilling it. So he said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"2387","57 - (2384) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: that a woman from Khatham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of sacrifice, and said: Allah's obligation of hajj has reached my father while he is a very old man unable to hold himself on the mount; do you see that we may perform hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"2388","58 - (2385) - And from Ibn Uyaynah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Walah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Any skin that is tanned has become pure."
"2389","59 - (2386) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I was among those whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead among the weak of his family from Muzdalifah to Mina."
"2390","60 - (2387) - And from Ibn Uyaynah, he said: Sulayman ibn Suhaym narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lifted the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and said: O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream that a Muslim sees or is seen for him. Verily I have been forbidden to recite bowing or prostrating; as for bowing, magnify the Lord in it, and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is fitting that you be answered."
"2391","61 - (2388) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I am amazed at one who starts the month early, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see it, fast; and when you see it, break; and if it is obscured from you, complete the count as thirty."
"2392","62 - (2389) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate on seven, and forbidden to gather his hair and clothes."
"2393","63 - (2390) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram."
"2394","64 - (2391) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, he heard Abu Mabad, he heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No man is alone with a woman, and no woman travels except with a mahram with her. So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was enrolled in such-and-such expedition, and my wife went out for hajj. He said: Go, perform hajj with your wife."
"2395","65 - (2392) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, he said: Abu Mabad informed me of this, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Then he denied it afterwards; from Ibn Abbas, he said: We used to recognize the end of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by the takbir."
"2396","66 - (2393) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram."
"2397","67 - (2394) - Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Abu al-Shatha, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah eight together and seven together."
"2398","68 - (2395) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, he said: Abu al-Shatha informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas; he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching: Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever does not find a waist-wrap, let him wear trousers."
"2399","69 - (2396) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching, saying: You will meet Allah barefoot, naked, walking, uncircumcised."
"2400","70 - (2397) - Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Amr reported to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Muhassab is nothing; it is only a place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped."
